CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in the presentation of foreign antigens to the
CC       immune system.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Heterodimer of an alpha chain and a beta chain (beta-2-
CC       microglobulin).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: The following alleles of B-51 are known: B*5101,
CC       B*5103, B*5104, B*5108 and B*5124. The sequence shown is that of
CC       B*5101.
CC   -!- DISEASE: HLA-B51 is associated with Behcet disease (BD)
CC       [MIM:109650]. BD is characterized by 4 major symptoms: oral
CC       aphthous ulcers, skin lesions, ocular symptoms, and genital
CC       ulcerations, and occasionally by inflammation in tissues and
CC       organs throughout the body, including the gastrointestinal tract,
CC       central nervous system, vascular system, lungs, and kidneys.
