CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in the presentation of foreign antigens to the
CC       immune system.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Heterodimer of an alpha chain and a beta chain (beta-2-
CC       microglobulin).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: The following alleles of Cw-6 are known: Cw*0602
CC       Cw*0603 and Cw*0604. The sequence shown is that of Cw*0602.
CC   -!- DISEASE: HLA-Cw*0602 is associated with psoriasis [MIM:177900].
CC       Psoriasis is a chronic inflammatory dermatosis that affects
CC       approximately 2% of the population. It is characterized by red,
CC       scaly skin lesions that are usually found on the scalp, elbows,
CC       and knees, and may be associated with severe arthritis. The
CC       lesions are caused by hyperproliferative keratinocytes and
CC       infiltration of inflammatory cells into the dermis and epidermis.
CC       The usual age of onset of psoriasis is between 15 and 30 years,
CC       although it can present at any age.
