CC   -!- FUNCTION: Plays a critical role in catalyzing the release of class
CC       II HLA-associated invariant chain-derived peptides (CLIP) from
CC       newly synthesized class II HLA molecules and freeing the peptide
CC       binding site for acquisition of antigenic peptides.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Heterodimer of an alpha chain (DMA) and a beta chain
CC       (DMB).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein. Localizes to late
CC       endocytic compartment. Associates with lysosome membranes.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: The following alleles of DMA are known: DMA*0101,
CC       DMA*0102, DMA*0103 (DMA3.2) and DMA*0104 (DMA3.4). The sequence
CC       shown is that of DMA*0101.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 immunoglobulin-like domain.
