CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the oxidation of nitroalkanes to produce the
CC       corresponding carbonyl compounds. It acts on 2-nitropropane better
CC       than on nitroethane and 1-nitropropane, and anionic forms of
CC       nitroalkanes are much better substrates than are neutral forms.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: 2 2-nitropropane + O(2) = 2 acetone + 2
CC       nitrite.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FMN.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Some, to FAD-dependent 2-nitropropane dioxygenase.
