CC   -!- FUNCTION: The 3beta-HSD enzymatic system plays a crucial role in
CC       the biosynthesis of all classes of hormonal steroids. HSD IV can
CC       only catalyze the conversion of dihydrotestosterone to 5 alpha-
CC       androstanediol in the presence of the cofactor NADPH. Exhibits
CC       only 3-ketosteroid reductase activity in the presence of NADPH and
CC       does not function as an isomerase.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: 3-beta-hydroxy-delta(5)-steroid + NADP(+) = 3-
CC       oxo-delta(5)-steroid + NADPH.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Steroid biosynthesis.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum and mitochondrial
CC       membrane-bound protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed predominantly in male liver.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the 3beta-HSD family.
