CC   -!- FUNCTION: Inhibits the auto- and transphosphorylation activity of
CC       BTK. Plays a negative regulatory role in BTK-related cytoplasmic
CC       signaling in B cells. Maybe involved in BCR-induced apoptotic cell
CC       death.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with BTK. Interacts with all isoforms of MAPK8,
CC       MAPK9, MAPK10 and MAPK12.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in testis and ovaries. It is
CC       also expressed in a variety of tissues including spleen, lymph
CC       node, thymus, bone marrow, fetal liver, colon, small intestine and
CC       prostate.
