RA   Muscatelli F., Mattei M.-G., Hen R.;
RT   "Mouse 5-hydroxytryptamine5A and 5-hydroxytryptamine5B receptors
RT   define a new family of serotonin receptors: cloning, functional
RT   expression, and chromosomal localization.";
RL   Mol. Pharmacol. 43:313-319(1993).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: This is one of the several different receptors for 5-
CC       hydroxytryptamine (serotonin), a biogenic hormone that functions
CC       as a neurotransmitter, a hormone, and a mitogen. The activity of
CC       this receptor is mediated by G proteins. Probably involved in
CC       anxiety and depression.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed predominantly in the central nervous
CC       system; in the hippocampus, habenula, and the doral raphe.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 1 of G-protein coupled receptors.
CC       STRONGEST TO THE OTHER 5HT-5 SUBTYPE RECEPTORS.
