CC   -!- FUNCTION: Dephosphorylates the 5' and 2'(3')-phosphates of
CC       deoxyribonucleotides and has a broad substrate specificity. Helps
CC       to regulate adenosine levels in heart during ischemia and hypoxia.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: A 5'-ribonucleotide + H(2)O = a ribonucleoside
CC       + phosphate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Magnesium.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Activated by ADP.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in skeletal muscle. Detected
CC       at intermediate levels in heart, brain, kidney and pancreas.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the 5' nucleotidase type 3 family.
