CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Heart, brain, liver and prostate, but not in
CC       kidney, lung, adrenal, aorta and pituitary. Isoform 4 is the most
CC       abundant isoform expressed in the prostate with high levels also
CC       detected in liver and heart.
CC   -!- PTM: Carboxyl-terminal Ser or Thr residues may be phosphorylated
CC       (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 1 of G-protein coupled receptors.
