CC   -!- FUNCTION: Could inhibit both insulin-receptor tyrosine kinase
CC       activity and insulin-stimulated receptor autophosphorylation and,
CC       concomitantly, antagonize the mitogenic effect of the hormone in
CC       cultured rat hepatoma cells.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Synthesized in liver and secreted by the
CC       hepatocytes in the blood.
CC   -!- PTM: Undergoes complex posttranslational modification involving N-
CC       glycosylation, and addition of fucose and sialic acid residues.
CC       Phosphorylation occurs at a serine residue.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the fetuin family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 cystatin-like domains.
