CC   -!- FUNCTION: Component of the adaptor complexes which link clathrin
CC       to receptors in coated vesicles. Clathrin-associated protein
CC       complexes are believed to interact with the cytoplasmic tails of
CC       membrane proteins, leading to their selection and concentration.
CC       Ap47 is a subunit of the plasma membrane adaptor.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Assembly protein complex 1 (AP-1) is a heterotetramer
CC       composed of two large chains (gamma and beta'), a medium chain
CC       (AP47) and a small chain (AP19).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Component of the coat surrounding the
CC       cytoplasmic face of coated vesicles located at the Golgi complex.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adaptor complexes medium subunit
CC       family.
