CC   -!- FUNCTION: Subunit of novel type of clathrin-or non-clathrin-
CC       associated protein coat involved in targeting proteins from the
CC       trans-Golgi network (TGN) to the endosomal-lysosomal system.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Adapter-like complex 4 (AP-4) is an heterotetramer
CC       composed of two large chains (epsilon/AP4E1 and beta/AP4B1), a
CC       medium chain (mu/AP4M1) and a small chain (sigma/AP4S1).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Associated with the trans-Golgi network.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Ubiquitous. Highly expressed in testis and
CC       lowly expressed in brain and lung.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: Interacts specifically with tyrosine-based sorting
CC       signals.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adaptor complexes medium subunit
CC       family.
