CC   -!- FUNCTION: Proteins of the antigen 85 complex are responsible for
CC       the high affinity of mycobacteria to fibronectin. Possesses a
CC       mycolyltransferase activity required for the biogenesis of
CC       trehalose dimycolate (cord factor), a dominant structure necessary
CC       for maintaining cell wall integrity (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- PTM: Contains one disulfide bridge (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the mycobacterial A85 antigen family.
