CC   -!- FUNCTION: Receptor for adenosine. The activity of this receptor is
CC       mediated by G proteins which inhibits adenylyl cyclase. Possible
CC       role in reproduction.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Most abundant in lung, spleen and pineal
CC       gland. Moderate expression in brain, kidney and testis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 1 of G-protein coupled receptors.
