CC   -!- FUNCTION: Sodium-independent, high affinity transport of small
CC       neutral D- and L-amino acids. May play a role in the modulation of
CC       glutamatergic transmission through mobilization of D-serine at the
CC       glutamatergic synapse.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Disulfide-linked heterodimer with the amino acid
CC       transport protein SLC3A2/4F2hc (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Probable).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in brain, heart, kidney, liver,
CC       lung, pancreas, placenta, and skeletal muscle.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in SLC7A10 may be involved in cystinuria (CSNU)
CC       which arises from impaired transport of cystine and dibasic amino
CC       acids through the epithelial cells of the renal tubule and
CC       gastrointestinal tract. Three types of cystinuria have been
CC       described.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the amino acid-polyamine-organocation (APC)
CC       superfamily.
