CC       Tobramycin and kanamycin resistance is due to the ACC activity,
CC       specified by the first 170 aa, and the gentamicin resistance is
CC       due to the APH activity encoded by the C-terminal region of the
CC       protein.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: THE N-TERMINAL REGION IS HOMOLOGOUS TO STREPTOTHRICIN
CC       ACETYLTRANSFERASE FROM S.LAVENDULAE. THE C-TERMINAL REGION IS
CC       HOMOLOGOUS TO OTHER APHS, AND TO A VIOMYCIN PHOSPHOTRANSFERASE
CC       (VPH).
