RT   "Characterization of nuclear targeting signal of hepatitis delta
RT   antigen: nuclear transport as a protein complex.";
RL   J. Virol. 66:914-921(1992).
RN   [3]
RP   ISOPRENOID.
RX   PubMed=8617711; DOI=10.1074/jbc.271.9.4569;
RA   Otto J.C., Casey P.J.;
RT   "The hepatitis delta virus large antigen is farnesylated both in vitro
RT   and in animal cells.";
RL   J. Biol. Chem. 271:4569-4572(1996).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Binds specifically to HDV RNA. The large form is
CC       required for packaging of the HDV ribonucleoprotein with hepatitis
CC       B surface antigen and inhibits viral RNA replication, whereas the
CC       small form is required for viral replication.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- PTM: Prenylation of HDAg-L is required for the assembly of viral
CC       particles.
CC   -!- PTM: Phosphorylated (By similarity).
CC   -!- RNA EDITING: Modified_positions=196; Note=Partially edited. RNA
CC       editing at this position occurs on the antigenomic strand and
CC       consists of a conversion of A to G catalyzed by the cellular
CC       enzyme ADAR1. The unedited RNA version gives rise to the small
CC       delta antigen, which ends with a nonsense codon at position 196.
CC       In the edited version, this amber codon is modified to a
CC       tryptophan codon and gives rise to the large delta antigen
CC       protein. HDAg-S suppresses editing of nonreplicating antigenomic
CC       RNA, thereby regulating the extent of editing (By similarity).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: The farnesyltransferase inhibitors BZA-5B and FTI-
CC       277 prevent the production of complete, infectious virions and are
CC       therefore antiviral agents against HDV (By similarity).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Binds specifically to antisera from patients with
CC       chronic hepatitis delta viral infections.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: This strain belongs to the genotype I found in
CC       North America, Europe, Africa, East and West Asia and the South
CC       Pacific.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the hepatitis delta antigen family.
