CC   -!- FUNCTION: Plays a role in lysophospholipid acylation. Transfers
CC       fatty acids to the 1-position via an enzyme-bound acyl-ACP
CC       intermediate in the presence of ATP and Mg(2+). Its physiological
CC       function is to regenerate PtdEtn from 2-acyl-GPE formed by
CC       transacylation reactions or degradation by phospholipase A1.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Inner membrane.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ATP-dependent AMP-binding enzyme
CC       family.
