CC   -!- FUNCTION: DNA deaminase (cytidine deaminase) that mediates a form
CC       of innate resistance to retroviral infections (at least to HIV-1
CC       infection) by triggering G-to-A hypermutation in the newly
CC       synthetized viral DNA. The replacements C-to-U in the minus strand
CC       DNA of HIV-1 during reverse transcription, leads to G-to-A
CC       transitions in the plus strand. The inhibition of viral
CC       replication is either due to the degradation of the minus strand
CC       before its integration or to the lethality of the hypermutations.
CC       Modification of both DNA strands is not excluded. This antiviral
CC       activity is neutralized by the virion infectivity factor (VIF),
CC       that prevents the incorporation of APOBEC3G into progeny HIV-1
CC       virions by both inhibiting its translation and/or by inducing its
CC       ubiquitination and subsequent degradation by the 26S proteasome.
CC       APOBEC3G binds a variety of RNAs, but does not display detectable
CC       APOB, NF1 and NAT1 mRNA editing.
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in hepatitis B virus (HBV) resistance probably
CC       primarily by inhibiting viral pregenomic RNA packaging. This
CC       activity is independent of the cytidine deaminase activity, as the
CC       inactivated protein is able to inhibit HBV replication. During HBV
CC       infection, APOBEC3G does not seem to be involved in the editing of
CC       HBV DNA, but this might occur in particular cellular contexts or
CC       with specific viral strains.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Zinc.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer. Interacts with APOBEC3B and HIV-1 VIF in a
CC       species specific manner.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mainly cytoplasmic. Small amount are found
CC       in the nucleus. During HIV-1 infection, virion-encapsidated in
CC       absence of HIV-1 VIF.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q9HC16-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q9HC16-2; Sequence=VSP_009587, VSP_009590;
CC         Note=May be due to a competing donor and acceptor splice sites
CC         and intron retentions. No experimental confirmation available;
CC       Name=3;
CC         IsoId=Q9HC16-3; Sequence=VSP_009588, VSP_009589;
CC         Note=May be due to a competing donor splice site;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in spleen, testes, ovary and
CC       peripheral blood leukocytes and CD4+ lymphocytes. Also expressed
CC       in non-permissive peripheral blood mononuclear cells, and several
CC       tumor cell lines; no expression detected in permissive lymphoid
CC       and non-lymphoid cell lines. Normally not expressed in the liver,
CC       but it is possible that it is induced in the course of HBV
CC       infection, for instance under the influence of cytokines.
CC   -!- PTM: Ubiquitinated in the presence of HIV-1 VIF. Association with
CC       VIF targets the protein for proteolysis by the ubiquitin-dependent
CC       proteasome pathway.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Inhibits also the infectivity of retroviral
CC       particles only distantly related to HIV-1, such as the simian
CC       immunodeficiency virus (SIV), the equine infectious anemia virus
CC       (EIAV) and the murine leukemia virus (MLV).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: HIV-1 does not replicate productively in nonhuman
CC       primates with the exception of the chimpanzee. The primates
CC       APOBEC3G (rhesus macaque, chimpanzee and African green monkey) are
CC       active against HIV-1 without VIF. Only the chimpanzee APOBEC3G is
CC       inhibited by HIV-1 VIF.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Accumulation of APOBEC3G induced non-lethal
CC       hypermutation could contribute to the genetic variation of primate
CC       lentiviral populations.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: It is one of seven related genes or pseudogenes
CC       found in a cluster, thought to result from gene duplication, on
CC       chromosome 22.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cytidine and deoxycytidylate deaminase
CC       family.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.4 (CAB45274) sequence differs from that shown due to
CC       erroneous gene model prediction.
CC   -!- DATABASE: NAME=Protein Spotlight; NOTE=Issue 45 of April 2004;
CC       WWW="http://www.expasy.org/spotlight/articles/sptlt045.html".
