CC   -!- FUNCTION: Controls temporal and spatial specificity in Aspergillus
CC       development. Expression of abaA leads to activation of brlA and
CC       wetA, cessation of vegetative growth, and accentuated cellular
CC       vacuolization. BrlA, abaA and wetA are pivotal regulators of
CC       conidiophore development and conidium maturation. They act
CC       individually and together to regulate their own expression and
CC       that of numerous other sporulation-specific genes.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 TEA DNA-binding domain.
