CC   -!- FUNCTION: This protein has a dual function: it suppresses a
CC       cytochrome b mRNA translation defect and is essential for the
CC       electron transfer in the bc1 complex. It is possible that ABC1 is
CC       involved in the correct folding and/or assembly of cytochrome B
CC       and that this folding occurs during the translation process.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial (Probable).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC1 family.
