CC   -!- FUNCTION: Could be involved in the transport of heme from the
CC       mitochondria to the cytosol. Plays a central role in the
CC       maturation of cytosolic iron-sulfur (Fe/S) cluster-containing
CC       proteins.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer or heterodimer (Potential).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Mitochondrial
CC       inner membrane (Potential).
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ABCB7 are the cause of X-linked sideroblastic
CC       anemia with ataxia (ASAT) [MIM:301310]. ASAT is a recessive
CC       disorder characterized by an infantile to early childhood onset of
CC       nonprogressive cerebellar ataxia and mild anemia with hypochromia
CC       and microcytosis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. MDR subfamily.
