RT   "Characterization and functional analysis of the nucleotide binding
RT   fold in human peroxisomal ATP binding cassette transporters.";
RL   FEBS Lett. 492:66-72(2001).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable transporter. The nucleotide-binding fold acts
CC       as an ATP-binding subunit with ATPase activity.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Can form heterodimers with ABCD1/ALD and ABCD2/ALDR.
CC       Dimerization is necessary to form an active transporter.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Peroxisomal.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ABCD3 may be the cause of Zellweger syndrome-2
CC       (ZWS-2) [MIM:170995]. ZWS-2 is an autosomal recessive disorder due
CC       to defective import mechanisms for peroxisomal matrix enzymes. The
CC       clinical phenotype includes characteristic facies, progressive
CC       neurological dysfunction, liver disease and death in infancy.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. ALD subfamily.
