OG   Plasmid IncI1 ColIb.
OC   Bacteria; Proteobacteria; Gammaproteobacteria; Enterobacteriales;
OC   Enterobacteriaceae; Escherichia.
OX   NCBI_TaxID=562;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A.
RC   STRAIN=K12;
RX   MEDLINE=89221310; PubMed=3072577;
RA   Gupta S.K., McCorquodale D.J.;
RT   "Nucleotide sequence of a DNA fragment that contains the abi gene of
RT   the ColIb plasmid.";
RL   Plasmid 20:194-206(1988).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: ABI may interact with a target in the cell membrane,
CC       which could be the product of the host's cmrA gene, and cause
CC       disruption of the cellular membrane such that lysis of the
CC       infected cell and death of the infecting phage would result.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: This very hydrophobic protein could insert
CC       itself into membranes.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: When phage T5 or its close relative BF23, infects
CC       cells harboring a ColIb plasmid, the infection is abortive. The
CC       mechanism involves gene products from the phage, the ColIb
CC       plasmid, and the host.
