RP   DNA C TO U EDITING ACTIVITY, AND TISSUE SPECIFICITY.
RX   MEDLINE=22744372; PubMed=12859895; DOI=10.1016/S0092-8674(03)00515-4;
RA   Mariani R., Chen D., Schroefelbauer B., Navarro F., Koenig R.,
RA   Bollman B., Muenk C., Nymark-McMahon H., Landau N.R.;
RT   "Species-specific exclusion of APOBEC3G from HIV-1 virions by Vif.";
RL   Cell 114:21-31(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable human APOBEC3G ortholog. Has DNA deaminase
CC       (cytidine deaminase) activity. Mediates G-to-A hypermutation in
CC       newly synthetized HIV-1 viral DNA and is thus able to prevent HIV-
CC       1 infectivity in vitro, in the presence and absence of HIV-1 VIF
CC       (virion infectivity factor).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Zinc (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mainly cytoplasmic. Small amount are found
CC       in the nucleus (By similarity).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=4;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q99J72-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q99J72-2; Sequence=VSP_009832;
CC       Name=3;
CC         IsoId=Q99J72-3; Sequence=VSP_009831, VSP_009833;
CC       Name=4;
CC         IsoId=Q99J72-4; Sequence=VSP_009831;
CC         Note=Lacks exon V. Also active in inhibiting HIV-1 in vitro;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in spleen, node and lung.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: Polymorphism seems to be an important factor for the
CC       ability of the protein to prevent HIV-1 infectivity in vitro. The
CC       protein derived from MDTF and EL4 cell lines are unable to reduce
CC       HIV-1 infectivity, while the protein derived from L1.2, 3T3 and
CC       splenocytes are able to do it, in the presence and absence of HIV-
CC       1 VIF (virion infectivity factor).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: HIV-1 VIF (virion infectivity factor) does not bind
CC       to mouse APOBEC3.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cytidine and deoxycytidylate deaminase
CC       family.
