CC   -!- FUNCTION: The dimeric enzyme activates NEDD8 by first adenylating
CC       its C-terminal glycine residue with ATP and thereafter linking
CC       this residue to the side chain of a cysteine residue on UBE1C,
CC       yielding a NEDD8-UBE1C thiolester and free AMP. Necessary for cell
CC       cycle progression through the S-M checkpoint. Overexpression of
CC       APPBP1 causes apoptosis through deregulation of NEDD8 conjugation
CC       (By similarity).
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Binding of TP53BP2 to the regulatory subunit
CC       APPBP1 decreases neddylation activity (By similarity).
CC   -!- PATHWAY: NEDD8 conjugation; first step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Heterodimer of UBE1C and APPBP1. The complex binds NEDD8.
CC       Binds APP and TP53BP2 (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Colocalizes with APP in lipid rafts (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: APPBP1 and UBE1C correspond to the N-terminal and
CC       the C-terminal part of yeast UBA3. In yeast the two subunits form
CC       a single polypeptide chain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ubiquitin-activating E1 family.
