CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the degradation of compounds such as
CC       putrescine, histamine, spermine, and spermidine, substances
CC       involved in allergic and immune responses, cell proliferation,
CC       tissue differentiation, tumor formation, and possibly apoptosis.
CC       Placental DAO is thought to play a role in the regulation of the
CC       female reproductive function.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: RCH(2)NH(2) + H(2)O + O(2) = RCHO + NH(3) +
CC       H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 copper ion and 1 topaquinone per subunit.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer; disulfide-linked.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Extracellular.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=P19801-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2; Synonyms=DAO2;
CC         IsoId=P19801-2; Sequence=VSP_006548;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Placenta and kidney.
CC   -!- PTM: Topaquinone (TPQ) is generated by copper-dependent
CC       autoxidation of a specific tyrosyl residue.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the copper/topaquinone oxidase family.
