RT   "Mutant analysis of interaction of the Bacillus subtilis transcription
RT   regulator AbrB with the antibiotic biosynthesis gene tycA.";
RL   FEBS Lett. 287:153-156(1991).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Ambiactive repressor and activator of the transcription
CC       of genes expressed during the transition state between vegetative
CC       growth and the onset of stationary phase and sporulation. It
CC       controls the expression of genes spovG and tycA. AbrB binds to the
CC       tycA promoter region at two A- and T-rich sites, it may be the
CC       sole repressor of tycA transcription.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Strong, to B.subtilis ABH and spoVT.
CC   -!- CAUTION: It is uncertain whether Met-1 or Met-3 is the initiator.
CC   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
