CC   -!- FUNCTION: Converts acetate to acetyl-CoA so that it can be used
CC       for oxidation through the tricarboxylic cycle to produce ATP and
CC       CO(2) (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + acetate + CoA = AMP + diphosphate +
CC       acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial matrix (By similarity).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q9NUB1-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q9NUB1-2; Sequence=VSP_007249;
CC         Note=No experimental confirmation available;
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ATP-dependent AMP-binding enzyme
CC       family.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.1 (CAB81884) sequence differs from that shown due to
CC       erroneous gene model prediction.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.3 sequence differs from that shown due to a
CC       frameshift in position 250 and numerous sequencing errors.
