CC   -!- FUNCTION: Converts acetate to acetyl-CoA so that it can be used
CC       for oxidation through the tricarboxylic cycle to produce ATP and
CC       CO(2).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + acetate + CoA = AMP + diphosphate +
CC       acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial matrix.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in heart, testis, kidney,
CC       skeletal muscle, lung and spleen. Detected at low levels in brain.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By fasting.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ATP-dependent AMP-binding enzyme
CC       family.
