CC   -!- FUNCTION: This magnesium-dependent enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis
CC       of ATP coupled with the translocation of calcium from the cytosol
CC       into the endoplasmic reticulum (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + H(2)O + Ca(2+)(Cis) = ADP + phosphate +
CC       Ca(2+)(Trans).
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Activated by calmodulin (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The N-terminus contains an autoinhibitory calmodulin-
CC       binding domain, which binds calmodulin in a calcium-dependent
CC       fashion (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cation transport ATPases family (P-type
CC       ATPases). Subfamily IIB.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.1 (CAB43665) sequence differs from that shown due to
CC       erroneous gene model prediction.
