CC   -!- FUNCTION: Putative subunit of the beta-cell ATP-sensitive
CC       potassium channel (KATP). Regulator of ATP-sensitive K+ channels
CC       and insulin release.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Associates with KCNJ11.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q09428-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q09428-2; Sequence=VSP_000055;
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ABCC8 are a cause of persistent
CC       hyperinsulinemic hypoglycemia of infancy (PHHI) [MIM:601820,
CC       256450]; also referred to as familial or congenital
CC       hyperinsulinism. PHHI is an autosomal recessive disorder
CC       characterized by unregulated and high insulin secretion. It causes
CC       nesidioblastosis, a diffuse abnormality of the pancreas in which
CC       there is extensive, often disorganized formation of new islets.
CC       PHHI has a variable clinical phenotype but usually presents during
CC       the neonatal period or infancy with seizures, coma, and often
CC       large birth weight for gestational age. Also dominantly inherited
CC       forms are known.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ABCC8 may contribute to non-insulin-dependent
CC       diabetes mellitus (NIDDM), also known as type II diabetes
CC       mellitus, in Northern European Caucasians.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. MRP subfamily.
