RA   Bienengraeber M., Olson T.M., Selivanov V.A., Kathmann E.C.,
RA   O'Cochlain F., Gao F., Karger A.B., Ballew J.D., Hodgson D.M.,
RA   Zingman L.V., Pang Y.-P., Alekseev A.E., Terzic A.;
RT   "ABCC9 mutations identified in human dilated cardiomyopathy disrupt
RT   catalytic KATP channel gating.";
RL   Nat. Genet. 36:382-387(2004).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Subunit of ATP-sensitve potassium channels (KATP). Can
CC       form cardiac and smooth muscle-type KATP channels with KIR6.2.
CC       KIR6.2 forms the channel pore while SUR2 is required for
CC       activation and regulation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=SUR2A;
CC         IsoId=O60706-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=SUR2B;
CC         IsoId=O60706-2; Sequence=VSP_000058;
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ABCC9 are the cause of dilated cardiomyopathy
CC       10 (CMD10) [MIM:608569]; also known as dilated cardiomyopathy with
CC       ventricular tachycardia.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. MRP subfamily.
