RT   putative drug-binding subunit of cardiac, skeletal muscle, and
RT   vascular KATP channels.";
RL   Diabetes 45:1439-1445(1996).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Subunit of ATP-sensitve potassium channels (KATP). Can
CC       form cardiac and smooth muscle-type KATP channels with KIR6.2.
CC       KIR6.2 forms the channel pore while SUR2 is required for
CC       activation and regulation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;
CC       Name=SUR2A;
CC         IsoId=P70170-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=SUR2B;
CC         IsoId=P70170-2; Sequence=VSP_000060;
CC       Name=SUR2C;
CC         IsoId=P70170-3; Sequence=VSP_000059;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Isoforms SUR2A and SUR2B are found in
CC       cerebellum, eye, atrium, ventricle, urinary bladder and skeletal
CC       muscle. Isoform SUR2B is also found in forebrain, liver, lung,
CC       pancreas, kidney, spleen, stomach, small intestine, colon, uterus,
CC       ovary and fat tissue. Isoform SUR2C is expressed exclusively in
CC       the heart.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. MRP subfamily.
