CC   -!- FUNCTION: This protein is a component of the acetyl coenzyme A
CC       carboxylase complex; first, biotin carboxylase catalyzes the
CC       carboxylation of the carrier protein and then the transcarboxylase
CC       transfers the carboxyl group to form malonyl-CoA.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + acetyl-CoA + HCO(3)(-) = ADP + phosphate
CC       + malonyl-CoA.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Acetyl-CoA carboxylase is an heterohexamer of biotin
CC       carboxyl carrier protein, biotin carboxylase and the two subunits
CC       of carboxyl transferase in a 2:2 complex.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the accD / PCCB family.
