RP   IDENTIFICATION IN ARC COMPLEX, AND SEQUENCE OF 50-61; 70-80 AND
RP   345-355.
RX   MEDLINE=99249346; PubMed=10235267; DOI=10.1038/19789;
RA   Naeaer A.M., Beaurang P.A., Zhou S., Abraham S., Solomon W.B.,
RA   Tjian R.;
RT   "Composite co-activator ARC mediates chromatin-directed
RT   transcriptional activation.";
RL   Nature 398:828-832(1999).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Has very high activity toward isobutyryl-CoA. Could be
CC       an isobutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase that functions in valine
CC       catabolism. Plays a role in transcriptional coactivation within
CC       the ARC complex.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Isobutyryl-CoA + ETF = methylacrylyl-CoA +
CC       reduced ETF.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD (By similarity).
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Valine catabolism.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Forms larger complexes inside the mitochonmdria,
CC       corresponding in size to tetramers. Subunit of the large
CC       multiprotein complexe ARC/DRIP.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Detected at comparable levels in all tissues
CC       examined (heart, lung, brain, skeletal muscle, pancreas and
CC       placenta). Weakly expressed in liver and kidney.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acyl-CoA dehydrogenase family.
