CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Butanoyl-CoA + acceptor = 2-butenoyl-CoA +
CC       reduced acceptor.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Mitochondrial fatty acid beta-oxidation system; first
CC       step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial matrix.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ACADS are the cause of short-chain acyl-CoA
CC       dehydrogenase deficiency (SCAD deficiency) [MIM:201470]. It is an
CC       autosomal recessive disorder resulting in acute acidosis and
CC       muscle weakness in infants, and a form of lipid-storage myopathy
CC       in adults.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: A number of straight-chain acyl-CoA dehydrogenases
CC       of different substrate specificities are present in mammalian
CC       tissues.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acyl-CoA dehydrogenase family.
