CC   -!- FUNCTION: Rapidly hydrolyzes choline released into the synapse. It
CC       can hydrolyze butyrylthiocholine.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Acetylcholine + H(2)O = choline + acetate.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Oligomer composed of disulfide-linked homodimers (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: May be secreted or membrane associated via a
CC       non-catalytic subunit.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Detected at all stages. Found to be more
CC       abundant in larval stages than in embryos or adults.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the type-B carboxylesterase/lipase family.
