CC   -!- FUNCTION: Trans-acting regulatory protein that activates
CC       transcription of the CUP1 gene (metallothionein) in response to
CC       copper ions. Binds to the CUP1 UAS sequence 5'-GCTTCTTTTCCGCTGA-
CC       3'. Binds DNA only in presence of copper or silver. Copper seems
CC       to alter the conformation of the protein.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 copper-fist DNA-binding domain.
