CC   -!- FUNCTION: Rapidly hydrolyzes choline released into the synapse.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Acetylcholine + H(2)O = choline + acetate.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer; composed of disulfide-linked homodimers.
CC       Catalytic forms H (GPI-anchor dimer) and T (asymmetric collagen-
CC       tailed), which differ in their C-terminus, account for all types
CC       of known ACHE forms. Interacts with PRIMA1. The interaction with
