CC   -!- FUNCTION: Fibrinolytic activity. Manifests an anticoagulant effect
CC       in human patients infected with L.achelous. Is sensible to serine
CC       proteinases and to thiol proteinases inhibitors.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Preferential cleavage of Arg-Gly bonds in all
CC       three fibrinogen chains.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Hemolymph and saliva of the larval form
CC       (caterpillar).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family S1.
