CC   -!- FUNCTION: After binding acetylcholine, the AChR responds by an
CC       extensive change in conformation that affects all subunits and
CC       leads to opening of an ion-conducting channel across the plasma
CC       membrane.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Neuronal AChR seems to be composed of two different types
CC       of subunits: alpha and non-alpha (beta). Alpha-2 subunit can be
CC       combined to beta-2 or beta-4 to give rise to functional receptors.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ligand-gated ionic channel (TC 1.A.9)
CC       family.
