CC   -!- FUNCTION: After binding acetylcholine, the AChR responds by an
CC       extensive change in conformation that affects all subunits and
CC       leads to opening of an ion-conducting channel across the plasma
CC       membrane.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Pentamer of two alpha chains, and one each of the beta,
CC       delta, and gamma (in immature muscle) or epsilon (in mature
CC       muscle) chains.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=P02708-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=P02708-2; Sequence=VSP_000071;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Isoform 1 is differentially expressed only in
CC       the skeletal muscle, whereas isoform 2 is constitutively expressed
CC       in skeletal muscle, brain, heart, kidney, liver lung and thymus.
CC   -!- DISEASE: The alpha subunit is the main focus for antibody binding
CC       in myasthenia gravis. Myasthenia gravis is characterized by
CC       sporadic muscular fatigability and weakness, occurring chiefly in
CC       muscles innervated by cranial nerves, and characteristically
CC       improved by cholinesterase-inhibiting drugs.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in CHRNA1 are a cause of the slow-channel
CC       congenital myasthenic syndrome (SCCMS) [MIM:601462, 254200]. SCCMS
CC       is an autosomal dominant form of congenital myasthenia gravis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ligand-gated ionic channel (TC 1.A.9)
CC       family.
