CC   -!- FUNCTION: After binding acetylcholine, the AChR responds by an
CC       extensive change in conformation that affects all subunits and
CC       leads to opening of an ion-conducting channel across the plasma
CC       membrane.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Neuronal AChR seems to be composed of two different type
CC       of subunits: alpha and beta.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in CHRNB2 are the cause of autosomal dominant
CC       nocturnal frontal lobe epilepsy type 3 (ENFL3) [MIM:605375]. It is
CC       a disease characterized by clusters of motor seizures during
CC       sleep.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ligand-gated ionic channel (TC 1.A.9)
CC       family.
