CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in the secretion of excess carbohydrate.
CC       Catalyzes interconversion of acetate and acetyl phosphate and
CC       appears to favor the formation of acetate.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + acetate = ADP + acetyl phosphate.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Induced by glucose excess, the induction may be
CC       mediated by ccpA transcriptional regulator.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Conversion of acetate to acetyl-CoA; first step.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acetokinase family.
