CC   -!- FUNCTION: Phosphorylates propionate (54%) in addition to acetate
CC       (100%). Uses GTP (100%), ITP (163%), UTP (56%), and CTP (21%) as
CC       phosphoryl donors in addition to ATP (100%).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + acetate = ADP + acetyl phosphate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Divalent cations. Manganese and magnesium are the most
CC       effective.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Conversion of acetate to acetyl-CoA; first step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic (By similarity).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Has a temperature optimum at 90 degrees Celsius.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the acetokinase family.
