RT   "A temperature-senstive strain of Histoplasma capsulatum has an
RT   altered D9-fatty acid desaturase gene.";
RL   Lipids 30:899-906(1995).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Utilizes O(2) and electrons from the reduced cytochrome
CC       b(5) domain to catalyze the insertion of a double bond into a
CC       spectrum of fatty acyl-CoA substrates.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Stearoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytrochrome b(5) + O(2)
CC       + 2 H(+) = oleoyl-CoA + 2 ferricytrochrome b(5) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Iron (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (By similarity).
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The histidine box domains may contain the active site
CC       and/or be involved in metal ion binding (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the fatty acid desaturase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 cytochrome b5 heme-binding domain.
