CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the formation of delta-11 fatty acyl
CC       precursors in the pheromone gland.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Stearoyl-CoA + AH(2) + O(2) = oleoyl-CoA + A +
CC       2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Iron (By similarity).
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Sex pheromone biosynthetic pathway.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum (By similarity).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Adult female pheromone gland. Increases by two
CC       or three orders of magnitude during the first 2 days after adult
CC       eclosion.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The histidine box domains may contain the active site
CC       and/or be involved in metal ion binding (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the fatty acid desaturase family.
