CC       cytochrome b5 to catalyze the insertion of a double bond into a
CC       spectrum of fatty acyl-CoA substrates among which palmitoyl-CoA
CC       and stearoyl-CoA (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Stearoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytrochrome b(5) + O(2)
CC       + 2 H(+) = oleoyl-CoA + 2 ferricytrochrome b(5) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Iron (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum (Probable).
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By cold. A 10-fold increase in transcript levels is
CC       observed 48-60 hours after cooling.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The histidine box domains may contain the active site
CC       and/or be involved in metal ion binding.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the fatty acid desaturase family.
