CC   -!- FUNCTION: This enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of the N-terminal
CC       peptide bond of an N-acetylated peptide to generate an N-
CC       acetylated amino acid and a peptide with a free N-terminus. It
CC       preferentially cleaves off Ac-Ala, Ac-Met and Ac-Ser.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Acylaminoacyl-peptide + H(2)O = acylamino acid
CC       + peptide.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- MASS SPECTROMETRY: MW=81269.9; MW_ERR=8.7; METHOD=Electrospray;
CC       RANGE=1-732; NOTE=Ref.5.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family S9C.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.4 sequence differs from that shown extensively due to
CC       frameshift errors.
