ID   ACT2_XENLA     STANDARD;      PRT;   377 AA.
AC   P10995;
DT   01-JUL-1989 (Rel. 11, Created)
DT   01-JUL-1989 (Rel. 11, Last sequence update)
DT   05-JUL-2004 (Rel. 44, Last annotation update)
DE   Actin, alpha sarcomeric/cardiac (Alpha 2).
OS   Xenopus laevis (African clawed frog).
OC   Eukaryota; Metazoa; Chordata; Craniata; Vertebrata; Euteleostomi;
OC   Amphibia; Batrachia; Anura; Mesobatrachia; Pipoidea; Pipidae;
OC   Xenopodinae; Xenopus.
OX   NCBI_TaxID=8355;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A.
RX   MEDLINE=88004409; PubMed=3653078;
RA   Stutz F., Spohr G.;
RT   "A processed gene coding for a sarcomeric actin in Xenopus laevis and
RT   Xenopus tropicalis.";
RL   EMBO J. 6:1989-1995(1987).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Actins are highly conserved proteins that are involved
CC       in various types of cell motility and are ubiquitously expressed
CC       in all eukaryotic cells.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Polymerization of globular actin (G-actin) leads to a
CC       structural filament (F-actin) in the form of a two-stranded helix.
CC       Each actin can bind to 4 others.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: In Xenopus laevis, three different alpha actins
CC       have been identified, a single smooth muscle actin and two
CC       sarcomeric forms that are preferentially expressed either in the
CC       heart or in the skeletal muscle. Each of these three alpha actin
CC       genes is present in at least two copies.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the actin family.
