RP   FUNCTION, AND INDUCTION.
RC   STRAIN=cv. Columbia;
RX   MEDLINE=21342503; PubMed=11449050;
RA   Kandasamy M.K., Gilliland L.U., McKinney E.C., Meagher R.B.;
RT   "One plant actin isovariant, ACT7, is induced by auxin and required
RT   for normal callus formation.";
RL   Plant Cell 13:1541-1554(2001).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Actins are highly conserved proteins that are involved
CC       in various types of cell motility and are ubiquitously expressed
CC       in all eukaryotic cells. Essential component of cell cytoskeleton;
CC       plays an important role in cytoplasmic streaming, cell shape
CC       determination, cell division, organelle movement and extension
CC       growth. This is considered as one of the vegetative actins which
CC       is involved in the regulation of hormone-induced plant cell
CC       proliferation and callus formation.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Polymerization of globular actin (G-actin) leads to a
CC       structural filament (F-actin) in the form of a two-stranded helix.
CC       The binding of profilin to monomeric G-actin cause the
CC       sequestration of actin into profilactin complexes, and prevents
CC       the polymerization.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Constitutively expressed at high levels in
CC       young expanding vegetative tissues. Also strongly expressed in the
CC       hypocotyl and seed coat. Little or no expression is detected in
CC       mature pollen sacs, ovules, embryos or seeds.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Differentially regulated in response to exogenous
CC       hormone treatment. In particular, auxin is a strong inducer.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are 8 actin genes in A.thaliana.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the actin family.
