CC   -!- FUNCTION: Receptor for ACTH. This receptor is mediated by G
CC       proteins (G(s)) which activate adenylate cyclase.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Melanocytes and corticoadrenal tissue.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in MC2R are the cause of glucocorticoid
CC       deficiency type 1 (GCCD1) [MIM:202200]; also known as familial
CC       glucocorticoid deficiency type 1 (FGD1). GCCD1 is an autosomal
CC       recessive disorder due to congenital insensitivity or resistance
CC       to adrenocorticotropin (ACTH). It is characterized by progressive
CC       primary adrenal insufficiency, without mineralocorticoid
CC       deficiency.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 1 of G-protein coupled receptors.
