CC   -!- FUNCTION: Cleaves the membrane-bound precursor of TNF-alpha at 76-
CC       Ala-|-Val-77 to its mature soluble form. Responsible for the
CC       proteolytic release of several other cell-surface proteins,
CC       including heparin binding epidermal growth-like factor, ephrin-A2
CC       and for constitutive and regulated alpha-secretase cleavage of
CC       amyloid precursor protein (APP). Contributes to the normal
CC       cleavage of the cellular prion protein. Involved in the cleavage
CC       of the adhesion molecule L1 at the cell surface and in released
CC       membrane vesicules, suggesting a vesicle-based protease activity.
CC       Controls also the proteolytic processing of Notch and mediates
CC       lateral inhibition during neurogenesis (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Endopeptidase of broad specificity.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with ephrin-A2 (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein. Is localized in the
CC       plasma membrane but is predominantly expressed in the Golgi
CC       apparatus and in released membrane vesicles derived likely from
CC       the Golgi.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in spleen, lymph node, thymus,
CC       peripheral blood leukocyte, bone marrow, cartilage and fetal
CC       liver.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: In osteoarthritis affected-cartilage.
CC   -!- PTM: The precursor is cleaved by a furin endopeptidase (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M12B.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 disintegrin domain.
