CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in skeletal muscle regeneration, specifically
CC       at the onset of cell fusion. Also involved in macrophage-derived
CC       giant cells (MGC) and osteoclast formation from mononuclear
CC       precursors.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with alpha-actinin-2 and with syndecans.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed during early developing mesenchymal
CC       cells that give rise to skeletal muscle, bones and visceral
CC       organs. Not expressed in adult normal muscle but expressed in
CC       regenerating muscle.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: At the onset of myoblast fusion.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The first 30 amino acids of the cytoplasmic domain contain
CC       a major binding site to alpha-actinin-2. This interaction is
CC       necessary to promote muscle cell fusion.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The cysteine-rich domain supports cell adhesion through
CC       syndecans and triggers signaling events that lead to beta-1
CC       integrin-dependent cell spreading. In carcinoma cells the binding
CC       of this domain to syndecans does not allow the integrin-mediated
CC       cell spreading (By similarity).
CC   -!- PTM: The precursor is cleaved by a furin endopeptidase (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Marker of skeletal muscle regeneration.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M12B.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 disintegrin domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 EGF-like domain.
