CC   -!- FUNCTION: Required for the function of some acidic activation
CC       domains, which activate transcription from a distant site. The
CC       exact mechanism of action is not yet known. ADA2, ADA3 and GCN5
CC       may function to acetylate nucleosomes opening up the promoter
CC       region.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with GCN5 and NR3C1. Associated with the P/CAF
CC       protein in the PCAF complex. Component of the PCAF complex, at
CC       least composed of TADA2L/ADA2, TADA3L/ADA3, TAF5L/PAF65beta,
CC       TAF6L/PAF65alpha, TAF10/TAFII30, TAF12/TAFII20, TAF9/TAFII31 and
CC       TRRAP.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in all tissues, but most abundantly
CC       in testis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 Myb-like domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 SWIRM domain.
