RP   IDENTIFICATION IN A SAGA COMPLEX WITH SPT7; HFI1; SPT8; GCN5; SPT20;
RP   SPT2; ADA2 AND TRA1.
RX   MEDLINE=99102959; PubMed=9885573; DOI=10.1016/S1097-2765(00)80300-7;
RA   Grant P.A., Schieltz D., Pray-Grant M.G., Yates J.R. III,
RA   Workman J.L.;
RT   "The ATM-related cofactor Tra1 is a component of the purified SAGA
RT   complex.";
RL   Mol. Cell 2:863-867(1998).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Transcription regulator. Could inhibits GAL4 DNA-binding
CC       or its ability to activate transcription. ADA2, ADA3 and GCN5 may
CC       function to acetylate nucleosomes opening up the promoter region.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Part of the ADA/GCN5 complex that consists of HFI1/ADA1,
CC       ADA2, ADA3, SPT20/ADA5 and GCN5. Component of the SAGA complex, a
CC       large multiprotein complex that modifies the chromatin, at least
CC       composed of SPT2, SPT7, SPT8, SPT20/ADA5, HFI1, ADA2, ADA3/NGG1,
CC       TRA1 and GCN5.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear (Potential).
