CC   -!- FUNCTION: Methylphosphotriester-DNA alkyltransferase is one of two
CC       genes required for the adaptive response of bacteria to alkylating
CC       agents. It accepts a methyl group from methylphospho-triesters and
CC       then acts as a transcriptional activator of the ada operon.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: One zinc ion per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 HTH araC/xylS-type DNA-binding domain.
