CC   -!- FUNCTION: Part of a complex that catalyzes the reversible cleavage
CC       of acetyl-CoA, allowing growth on acetate as sole source of carbon
CC       and energy (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Acetyl-CoA + [acetyl-CoA
CC       decarbonylase/synthase complex beta subunit] = CoA + acetyl-
CC       [acetyl-CoA decarbonylase/synthase complex beta subunit].
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 nickel-iron-sulfur cluster.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Methanogenesis from acetate; third step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer. The ACDS complex is made up of alpha, epsilon,
CC       beta, gamma and delta chains with a probable stoichiometry of
CC       (alpha(2)epsilon(2))(4)-beta(8)-(gamma(1)delta(1))(8) (Potential).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cdhC family.
