CC   -!- FUNCTION: Part of a complex that catalyzes the reversible cleavage
CC       of acetyl-CoA, allowing growth on acetate as sole source of carbon
CC       and energy. Probably maintains the overall quaternary structure of
CC       the ACDS complex (By similarity).
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Methanogenesis from acetate; third step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Heterodimer of delta and gamma chains. The ACDS complex
CC       is made up of alpha, epsilon, beta, gamma and delta chains with a
CC       probable stoichiometry of (alpha(2)epsilon(2))(4)-beta(8)-
CC       (gamma(1)delta(1))(8) (Potential).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the cdhD family.
