RA   Petersen C., Moeller L.B., Valentin-Hansen P.;
RT   "The cryptic adenine deaminase gene of Escherichia coli. Silencing by
RT   the nucleoid-associated DNA-binding protein, H-NS, and activation by
RT   insertion elements.";
RL   J. Biol. Chem. 277:31373-31380(2002).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Adenine + H(2)O = hypoxanthine + NH(3).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Manganese.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Repressed by H-NS. Activated by insertion of a variety
CC       of IS elements into a region extending from -145 to +13 relative
CC       to the transcription start site. IS elements essentially eliminate
CC       the H-NS-mediated silencing, but also stimulate ade expression 2-3
CC       fold independently of the H-NS protein.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimal pH is 6.5-7.0 and optimal temperature is 60
CC       degrees Celsius.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Ade is a cryptic gene in wild-type strains. The
CC       physiological conditions that lead to its activation are unknown.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adenine deaminase family.
