CC   -!- FUNCTION: Could function in retinol oxidation for the synthesis of
CC       retinoic acid, a hormone important for cellular differentiation.
CC       Medium-chain (octanol) and aromatic (m-nitrobenzaldehyde)
CC       compounds are the best substrates. Ethanol is not a good substrate
CC       but at the high ethanol concentrations reached in the digestive
CC       tract, it plays a role in the ethanol oxidation and contributes to
CC       the first pass ethanol metabolism.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An alcohol + NAD(+) = an aldehyde or ketone +
CC       NADH.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 2 zinc ions per subunit.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Preferentially expressed in stomach.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are 7 different ADH's isozymes in human:
CC       three belongs to class-I: alpha, beta, and gamma, one to class-II:
CC       pi, one to class-III: chi, one to class-IV: ADH7 and one to class-
CC       V: ADH6.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the zinc-containing alcohol dehydrogenase
CC       family. Class-IV subfamily.
