RT   ADH3*1.";
RL   Hepatology 31:984-989(2000).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An alcohol + NAD(+) = an aldehyde or ketone +
CC       NADH.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 2 zinc ions per subunit.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Dimer of identical or nonidentical chains of three types;
CC       alpha, beta and gamma.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: Three alleles are known: ADH1B*1 (ADH2*1)
CC       corresponding to variant beta-1, ADH1B*2 (ADH2*2) corresponding to
CC       variant beta-2, ADH1B*3 (ADH2*3) corresponding to variant beta-3.
CC       The sequence shown is that of allele ADH1B*1. The ADH1B*2 allele
CC       frequency in orientals is approximately 75%, whereas it is less
CC       than 5% in most Caucasian populations.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are 7 different ADH's isozymes in human:
CC       three belongs to class-I: alpha, beta, and gamma, one to class-II:
CC       pi, one to class-III: chi, one to class-IV: ADH7 and one to class-
CC       V: ADH6.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the zinc-containing alcohol dehydrogenase
CC       family.
