RP   VARIANTS GAMMA-2 GLN-271 AND VAL-349.
RX   MEDLINE=87004628; PubMed=3758060;
RA   Hoeoeg J.-O., Heden L.-O., Larsson K., Joernvall H.;
RT   "The gamma 1 and gamma 2 subunits of human liver alcohol
RT   dehydrogenase. cDNA structures, two amino acid replacements, and
RT   compatibility with changes in the enzymatic properties.";
RL   Eur. J. Biochem. 159:215-218(1986).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An alcohol + NAD(+) = an aldehyde or ketone +
CC       NADH.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 2 zinc ions per subunit.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Dimer of identical or nonidentical chains of three types;
CC       alpha, beta and gamma.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: Two main alleles are known, ADH3*1 or gamma-1 has
CC       Arg-271/Ile-349 while ADH3*2 or gamma-2 has Gln-271/Val-349.
CC       ADH3*1 is associated with a fast rate of ethanol oxidation and
CC       ADH3*2 with a slow rate.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are 7 different ADH's isozymes in human:
CC       three belongs to class-I: alpha, beta, and gamma, one to class-II:
CC       pi, one to class-III: chi, one to class-IV: ADH7 and one to class-
CC       V: ADH6.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the zinc-containing alcohol dehydrogenase
CC       family.
