CC   -!- FUNCTION: AM and PAMP are potent hypotensive and vasodilatator
CC       agents. Numerous actions have been reported most related to the
CC       physiologic control of fluid and electrolyte homeostasis. In the
CC       kidney, am is diuretic and natriuretic, and both am and pamp
CC       inhibit aldosterone secretion by direct adrenal actions. In
CC       pituitary gland, both peptides at physiologically relevant doses
CC       inhibit basal ACTH secretion. Both peptides appear to act in brain
CC       and pituitary gland to facilitate the loss of plasma volume,
CC       actions which complement their hypotensive effects in blood
CC       vessels.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highest levels found in pheochromocytoma and
CC       adrenal medulla. Also found in lung, ventricle and kidney tissues.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adrenomedullin family.
