CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An aldehyde + H(2)O + O(2) = a carboxylic acid
CC       + H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD, molybdopterin, and two 2Fe-2S clusters.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Abundant in liver, lower levels in lung,
CC       skeletal muscle, pancreas. Undetected in heart, brain and kidney.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the xanthine dehydrogenase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 2Fe-2S type ferredoxin domain.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Was originally (Ref.1) thought to be a xanthine
CC       dehydrogenase.
