CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An aldehyde + H(2)O + O(2) = a carboxylic acid
CC       + H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD, molybdopterin, and two 2Fe-2S clusters (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highest expression in esophagus. Moderately
CC       low expression in lung, liver, heart and testis. In brain,
CC       expression is very high in choroid plexus, high in hind brain and
CC       low in hippocampus and cerebellum. In spinal cord expression is
CC       strongest in anterior horns. Low expression detected in spleen and
CC       eye. Not detected in stomach, small intestine, large intestine,
CC       skin or striated muscle. AXO1 expression in the livers of mice is
CC       approximately seven times greater in males than females.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed in adult liver but not in neonatal
CC       or embryonic liver.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the xanthine dehydrogenase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 2Fe-2S type ferredoxin domain.
