CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An aldehyde + H(2)O + O(2) = a carboxylic acid
CC       + H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD, molybdopterin, and two 2Fe-2S clusters (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic (By similarity).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expression detected in liver, heart, lung,
CC       spleen and kidney.
CC   -!- PTM: The N-terminus is blocked.
CC   -!- POLYMORPHISM: The sequence variants between males and females may
CC       be due to differences between individual animals rather than true
CC       gender differences.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Male and female rats possess kinetically distinct
CC       forms of AXO1 which may be due to differences in redox states. The
CC       sequence shown here is that of a female.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the xanthine dehydrogenase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 2Fe-2S type ferredoxin domain.
