CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts on ADP-mannose and ADP-glucose as well as ADP-
CC       ribose. Prevents glycogen biosynthesis. The reaction catalyzed by
CC       this enzyme is a limiting step of the gluconeogenic process (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ADP-ribose + H(2)O = AMP + D-ribose 5-
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Requires divalent ions: magnesium, manganese or zinc.
CC       Binds 3 magnesium ions per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Inhibited by phosphorylated compounds such as
CC       AMP, ADP, ATP, 3-phosphoglyceric acid and PPi. Not inhibited by
CC       orthophosphate. Activity is high in cells grown in low glucose
CC       concentrations and decreases dramatically as glucose concentration
CC       increases (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the Nudix hydrolase family. NudF subfamily.
