CC   -!- FUNCTION: Disease resistance (R) protein that mediates resistance
CC       against Peronospora parasitica in a salicylic acid-dependent
CC       manner. Also mediates resistance against Erysiphe cichoracearum is
CC       both salicylic acid-dependent and partially NPR1-dependent.
CC       Resistance proteins guard the plant against pathogens that contain
CC       an appropriate avirulence protein via an indirect interaction with
CC       this avirulence protein. That triggers a defense system including
CC       the hypersensitive response, which restricts the pathogen growth.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Accumulates in leaves 1.5 hour postinfiltration of
CC       Pseudomonas syringae.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The LRR repeats probably act as specificity determinant of
CC       pathogen recognition (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the disease resistance NB-LRR family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 4 leucine-rich (LRR) repeats.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 NB-ARC domain.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.2 sequence differs from that shown due to erroneous
CC       gene model prediction.
CC   -!- DATABASE: NAME=NIB-LRRS;
CC       NOTE=Functional and comparative genomics of disease resistance gene
CC       homologs;
CC       WWW="http://niblrrs.ucdavis.edu".
