CC   -!- FUNCTION: Receptor for globular and full-length adiponectin
CC       (APM1), an essential hormone secreted by adipocytes that acts as
CC       an antidiabetic. Probably involved in metabolic pathways that
CC       regulate lipid metabolism such as fatty acid oxidation. Mediates
CC       increased AMPK, PPARA ligand activity, fatty acid oxidation and
CC       glucose uptake by adiponectin. Has some intermediate-affinity
CC       receptor activity for both globular and full-length adiponectin.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: May form homo and heteromultimers.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Localized to the
CC       cell membrane and intracelllar organelles.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in skeletal muscle, liver and
CC       placenta. Weakly expressed in brain, heart, colon, spleen, kidney,
CC       thymus, small intestine, peripheral blood leukocytes and lung.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ADIPOR family.
