CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable receptor, which is involved in metabolic
CC       pathways that regulate lipid metabolism such as fatty acid
CC       oxidation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Regulated by OAF1 and PIP2. Highly expressed in
CC       presence of glucose. Expressed at lower level in presence of
CC       glycerol or glycerol and oleate. Highly expressed in the presence
CC       of saturated fatty-acids such as myristate.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ADIPOR family.
