CC   -!- FUNCTION: Serves as the first electron transfer protein in all the
CC       mitochondrial p450 systems. Including cholesterol side chain
CC       cleavage in all steroidogenic tissues, steroid 11-beta
CC       hydroxylation in the adrenal cortex, 25-OH-vitamin D3-24
CC       hydroxylation in the kidney, and sterol C-27 hydroxylation in the
CC       liver.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Reduced ferredoxin + NADP(+) = oxidized
CC       ferredoxin + NADPH.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: FAD.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Cholesterol side-chain-cleavage system.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial matrix.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=Short;
CC         IsoId=P08165-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=Long;
CC         IsoId=P08165-2; Sequence=VSP_003415;
CC         Note=Represents 10-20% of all adrenodoxin reductase mRNAs and
CC         seems to be inactive;
