CC   -!- FUNCTION: Ca(2+)-dependent actin filament-severing protein that is
CC       presumed to have a regulatory function in exocytosis by affecting
CC       the organization of the microfilament network underneath the
CC       plasma membrane. In vitro, also has barbed end capping and
CC       nucleating activities in the presence of Ca(2+).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: In the adrenal gland, expressed in the medulla
CC       but, in the cortex, found only in diffuse parts.
CC   -!- PTM: The N-terminus is blocked.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the villin/gelsolin family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 6 gelsolin-like repeats.
