CC   -!- FUNCTION: Ca(2+)-regulated actin-binding protein. May have a
CC       unique function in the morphogenesis of neuronal cells which form
CC       ganglia.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Most highly expressed in the endometrium of
CC       the uterus, the intestinal villi and the testes. Weaker expression
CC       also detected in the brain and on the surface of the tongue.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Highest expression was detected in dorsal
CC       root and trigeminal ganglia by embryonic day 14.5 and continued
CC       through at least day 16.5.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the villin/gelsolin family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 6 gelsolin-like repeats.
