CC   -!- FUNCTION: Adrenodoxin transfer electrons from adrenodoxin
CC       reductase to the cholesterol side chain cleavage cytochrome P450.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 2Fe-2S cluster.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial matrix.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There is two copies of the adrenodoxin precursor
CC       which differ in positions 24 to 60 (the C-terminal of the transit
CC       peptide and the first two residues of the mature sequence).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the adrenodoxin / putidaredoxin family.
