RX   MEDLINE=21607787; PubMed=11742972; DOI=10.1093/emboj/20.24.6946;
RA   Moreno-Borchart A.C., Strasser K., Finkbeiner M.G., Shevchenko A.,
RA   Shevchenko A., Knop M.;
RT   "Prospore membrane formation linked to the leading edge protein (LEP)
RT   coat assembly.";
RL   EMBO J. 20:6946-6957(2001).
RN   [3]
RP   FUNCTION, SUBCELLULAR LOCATION, AND INTERACTIONS WITH SPO21, NUD1 AND
RP   CNM67.
RX   MEDLINE=21969403; PubMed=11973299;
RA   Nickas M.E., Neiman A.M.;
RT   "Ady3p links spindle pole body function to spore wall synthesis in
RT   Saccharomyces cerevisiae.";
RL   Genetics 160:1439-1450(2002).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in the pathway that organizes the prospore
CC       membrane (PSM) during sporulation. Mediates the assembly of the
CC       DON1 ring structure at the leading edge of PSM during meiosis II.
CC       May constitute a physical link between SSP1-containing PSM
CC       precursors and the spindle pole body (SPB) and may facilitate the
CC       recruitment of other factors that are required to promote spore
CC       wall formation.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts directly with SSP1. Probable component of a SPB
CC       complex composed of ADY3, SSP1, DON1, MPC54, SPO21/MPC70, NUD1 and
CC       CNM67.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Localizes to prospore membrane and SPB.
CC       Localizes to the leading edge, which cover the ring-shape opening
CC       of the PSMs during meiosis II. Colocalizes with DON1 to dots in
CC       the cytoplasm and at the SPB. Its localization to the PSMs but not
CC       to the SPBs depends on SSP1.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Meiosis-specific. Expressed from 3 to 9 hours
CC       after induction of sporulation. Not expressed during mitosis.
CC   -!- PTM: Phosphorylated.
