RP   FUNCTION.
RX   PubMed=14651850; DOI=10.1016/S0092-8674(03)00924-3;
RA   Benkova E., Michniewicz M., Sauer M., Teichmann T., Seifertova D.,
RA   Juergens G., Friml J.;
RT   "Local, efflux-dependent auxin gradients as a common module for plant
RT   organ formation.";
RL   Cell 115:591-602(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts as a component of the auxin efflux carrier. Seems
CC       to be involved in the basipetal auxin transport. Mediates the
CC       formation of auxin gradient which is required to ensure correct
CC       organogenesis. Coordinated polar localization of PIN1 is directly
CC       regulated by the vesicle trafficking process. The ARF-GEF protein
CC       GNOM is required for the correct recycling of PIN1 between the
CC       plasma membrane and endosomal compartments.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed at the basal side of elongated
CC       parenchymatous xylem cells.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed during embryogenesis. Already
CC       detected in the 8-cell stage at the inner cell boundaries. Later,
CC       polarity is gradually established at the basal side of provascular
CC       cells then in epidermis cells.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Loss-of-function mutants exibit developped naked,
CC       pin-shaped inflorescences and abnormalities in the number, size,
CC       shape, and position of lateral organs.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the auxin efflux carrier (TC 2.A.69)
CC       family.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.1 (AAD04377) sequence differs from that shown due to
CC       erroneous gene model prediction.
