RT   "Empirical analysis of transcriptional activity in the Arabidopsis
RT   genome.";
RL   Science 302:842-846(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts as a component of the auxin efflux carrier. Seems
CC       to be involved in the root-specific auxin transport, and mediates
CC       the root gravitropism. Its particular localization suggest a role
CC       in the translocation of auxin towards the elongation zone.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Root-specific. Localized to the cortex,
CC       epidermis and lateral root cap, predominantly at the upper side of
CC       cells.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Loss-of-function mutations impair the root
CC       gravitropic response, lead to an increased sensitivity to ethylene
CC       and auxin transport inhibitors, and give rise to an auxin
CC       accumulation in root tips.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the auxin efflux carrier (TC 2.A.69)
CC       family.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.5 sequence differs from that shown due to erroneous
CC       gene model prediction.
