RT   "Efflux-dependent auxin gradients establish the apical-basal axis of
RT   Arabidopsis.";
RL   Nature 426:147-153(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts as a component of the auxin efflux carrier. Seems
CC       to be involved in the lateral auxin transport system and mediates
CC       tropic growth. Coordinated polar localization of PIN3 is directly
CC       regulated by the vesicle trafficking process.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Predominantly expressed at the lateral side of
CC       shoot endodermis cells as well as root pericycle and columella
CC       cells.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed during embryogenesis. Detected in
CC       the precursors of the columella root cells.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Loss-of-function mutants display defects in
CC       hypocotyl differential growth.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the auxin efflux carrier (TC 2.A.69)
CC       family.
