CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts as a component of the auxin efflux carrier. Plays a
CC       role in generating a sink for auxin into columella cells.
CC       Maintains the endogenous auxin gradient, which is essential for
CC       correct root patterning.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q8RWZ6-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q8RWZ6-2; Sequence=VSP_009419;
CC         Note=May be due to a competing donor splice site. No
CC         experimental confirmation available;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in the quiescent center precursors
CC       and surrounding cells.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed during embryogenesis. Detected in
CC       the embryonic and seedling root meristems.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Loss-of-function mutants display altered patterning
CC       in the developing root meristem.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the auxin efflux carrier (TC 2.A.69)
CC       family.
