RP   FUNCTION, DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE, AND NULL MUTANTS ATPIN7.
RX   PubMed=14614497; DOI=10.1038/nature02085;
RA   Friml J., Vieten A., Sauer M., Weijers D., Schwarz H., Hamann T.,
RA   Offringa R., Juergens G.;
RT   "Efflux-dependent auxin gradients establish the apical-basal axis of
RT   Arabidopsis.";
RL   Nature 426:147-153(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acts as a component of the auxin efflux carrier.
CC       Mediates the initial auxin gradient which contributes to the
CC       establishment of the apical-basal axis in early embryogenesis.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q940Y5-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q940Y5-2; Sequence=VSP_009420, VSP_009421, VSP_009422;
CC         Note=May be due to a competing donor splice site and to an
CC         intron retention. No experimental confirmation available;
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed during early embryogenesis.
CC       Detected apically in the basal cell lineage resulting from the
CC       first zygotic division. At the 32-cell stage, localization shifts
CC       to the basal side of the cells in the developing embryo.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Loss-of-function mutants display altered embryo
CC       with defects in stereotypical pattern of early embryogenesis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the auxin efflux carrier (TC 2.A.69)
CC       family.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.2 sequence differs from that shown due to erroneous
CC       gene model prediction.
