RA   Fletcher H.M., Zhulin I.B., Taylor B.L.;
RT   "The Aer protein and the serine chemoreceptor Tsr independently sense
RT   intracellular energy levels and transduce oxygen, redox, and energy
RT   signals for Escherichia coli behavior.";
RL   Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A. 94:10541-10546(1997).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Signal transducer for aerotaxis. The aerotactic response
CC       is the accumulation of cells around air bubbles. The nature of the
CC       sensory stimulus detected by this protein is the proton motive
CC       force or cellular redox state. It uses a FAD prosthetic group as a
CC       redox sensor to monitor oxygen levels.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Inner membrane
CC       (Potential).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 methyl-accepting transducer domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 PAS (PER-ARNT-SIM) dimerization domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 PAS-associated C-terminal (PAC) domain.
