CC   -!- FUNCTION: Blocks mechanosensitive ion channels and the hypotonic
CC       cell swelling induced calcium increase associated with the
CC       activation of such channels. It can thus be useful in treating
CC       cardiac ventricular disturbances. Also induces analgesia in
CC       mammals. This analgesia is probably mediated by a non-opioid
CC       receptor related mechanism.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed by the venom gland.
CC   -!- MASS SPECTROMETRY: MW=3979.9; METHOD=Electrospray; RANGE=1-31;
CC       NOTE=Ref.1, Ref.2.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the spider potassium channel inhibitory
CC       toxin family.
