CC   -!- FUNCTION: Adds the eighth mannose residue in an alpha-1,6 linkage
CC       onto the dolichol-PP-oligosaccharide precursor (dolichol-PP-
CC       Man(7)GlcNAc(2)) required for protein glycosylation.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Glycosylation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum (Probable).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in fibroblasts.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ALG12 are the cause of congenital disorder of
CC       glycosylation type Ig (CDG-Ig) [MIM:607143]. Type I congenital
CC       disorders of glycosylation are diseases presenting multisystemic
CC       lesions including central and peripheral nervous system deficits.
CC       Clinically, most CDG patients present with psychomotor
CC       retardation, hypotonia, cerebellar hypoplasia, hormonal disorders
CC       and stroke-like episodes. The disease is characterized by under-
CC       glycosylated serum glycoproteins and is caused by mutations in
CC       genes encoding proteins involved in the stepwise assembly of
CC       dolichol-oligosaccharide used for protein N-glycosylation.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase family 22.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.2 sequence differs from that shown due to a
CC       frameshift in position 468.
