CC   -!- FUNCTION: Essential for lysis of subvacuolar cytoplasm to vacuole
CC       targeted bodies and intravacuolar autophagic bodies. Involved in
CC       the lysis of intravacuolar multivesicular body (MVB) vesicles.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Triacylglycerol + H(2)O = diacylglycerol + a
CC       fatty acid anion.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type II membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum. From ER, targeted to vacuolar lumen at the MVB vesicles
CC       via the Golgi and the prevacuolar compartment (PVC).
CC   -!- PTM: Glycosylated.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the AB hydrolase superfamily. Lipase
CC       family.
