CC   -!- FUNCTION: Mediates the cell surface attachment of the a-agglutinin
CC       subunit. S.cerevisiae a and alpha cells express the complementary
CC       cell surface glycoproteins a-agglutinin and alpha-agglutinin,
CC       respectively, which interact with one another to promote cellular
CC       aggregation during mating.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Contains at least a binding subunit disulfide-linked to a
CC       core subunit.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Attached to the membrane by a GPI-anchor
CC       and/or by carbohydrate-mediated covalent cross-links (Probable).
CC   -!- PTM: Extensively O-glycosylated.
