RA   Zhu A., Goldstein J.;
RT   "Cloning and functional expression of a cDNA encoding coffee bean
RT   alpha-galactosidase.";
RL   Gene 140:227-231(1994).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Preferentially cleaves alpha-1,3 and alpha-1,4 glycoside
CC       linkages. Involved in the hydrolysis of the galactomannan, it
CC       splits alpha-linked galactose moieties. It is particularly
CC       suitable for the hydrolysis of guar gum to a gum with improved
CC       gelling properties. Can cleave terminal alpha-1,3-linked galactose
CC       residues responsible for blood group B specificity from the
CC       surface of erythrocytes thereby converting these cells
