CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Melibiose + H(2)O = galactose + glucose.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Lysosomal.
CC   -!- RNA EDITING: Modified_positions=396; Note=Partially edited.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in GLA are the cause of Fabry's disease (FD)
CC       [MIM:301500]. FD is a rare X-linked sphingolipidosis disease where
CC       glycolipid accumulates in many tissues. Clinical recognition in
CC       males results from characteristic skin lesions (angiokeratomas)
CC       over the lower trunk. Patients may show ocular deposits, febrile
CC       episodes, and burning pain in the extremities. Death results from
CC       renal failure, cardiac or cerebral complications of hypertension
CC       or other vascular disease. Heterozygous females may exhibit the
CC       disorder in an attenuated form, they are more likely to show
CC       corneal opacities.
CC   -!- BIOTECHNOLOGY: Used to convert blood group antigens of type B into
CC       type O, the universal donor type.
CC   -!- PHARMACEUTICAL: Available under the names Replagal (Transkaryotic
CC       Therapies) and Fabrazyme (Genzyme). Used as a long-term enzyme
CC       replacement therapy in patients with a confirmed diagnosis of
CC       Fabry's disease.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 27 of glycosyl hydrolases.
