CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the reversible condensation of
CC       dihydroxyacetone phosphate with glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate to
CC       produce tagatose 1,6-bisphosphate.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: D-tagatose 1,6-bisphosphate 1,6-bisphosphate =
CC       glycerone-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: N-acetylgalactosamine utilization.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class II fructose-bisphosphate aldolase
CC       family.
