CC   -!- FUNCTION: This protein functions both as a chitinase and as a N-
CC       acetyl-D-glucosamine binding lectin. It inhibits the growth of
CC       several phytopathogenic chitin-containing fungi. Possesses also
CC       insecticidal activity.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Hydrolysis of the 1,4-beta-linkages of N-
CC       acetyl-D-glucosamine polymers of chitin.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Rhizomes and inflorescence with immature
CC       seeds.
CC   -!- PTM: Proteolytically processed to yield a very small protein (8.5
CC       kDa, 86 AA) containing only the two chitin-binding domains.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 chitin-binding domains.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 chitin-binding type-1 domains.
