RN   [5]
RP   FUNCTION.
RX   MEDLINE=20115426; PubMed=10648231;
RA   Ferrandiz C., Gu Q., Martienssen R., Yanofsky M.F.;
RT   "Redundant regulation of meristem identity and plant architecture by
RT   FRUITFULL, APETALA1 and CAULIFLOWER.";
RL   Development 127:725-734(2000).
RN   [6]
RP   FUNCTION.
RX   PubMed=15035986; DOI=10.1016/S0092-8674(04)00217-X;
RA   Liljegren S.J., Roeder A.H.K., Kempin S.A., Gremski K., Ostergaard L.,
RA   Guimil S., Reyes D.K., Yanofsky M.F.;
RT   "Control of fruit patterning in Arabidopsis by INDEHISCENT.";
RL   Cell 116:843-853(2004).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable transcription factor that promotes early floral
CC       meristem identity in synergy with APETALA1 and CAULIFLOWER. Is
CC       required subsequently for the transition of an inflorescence
CC       meristem into a floral meristem. Seems to be partially redundant
CC       to the function of APETALA1 and CAULIFLOWER in the up-regulation
CC       of LEAFY. Is also required for normal pattern of cell division,
CC       expansion and differentiation during morphogenesis of the silique.
CC       Probably not required for fruit elongation but instead is required
CC       to prevent ectopic activity of IND.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer capable of binding to CArG-box sequences (By
CC       similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear (By similarity).
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Vascular tissue of cauline leaves, floral
CC       shoot apex and valves of carpels and fruits.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Dramatically up-regulated upon the transition from
CC       vegetative to reproductive development.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 K-box dimerization domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 MADS-box domain.
