GN   Name=aglB;
OS   Klebsiella pneumoniae.
OC   Bacteria; Proteobacteria; Gammaproteobacteria; Enterobacteriales;
OC   Enterobacteriaceae; Klebsiella.
OX   NCBI_TaxID=573;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A., SEQUENCE OF 1-26, AND MASS SPECTROMETRY.
RC   STRAIN=ATCC 23357;
RX   MEDLINE=21463057; PubMed=11473129; DOI=10.1074/jbc.M106504200;
RA   Thompson J., Robrish S.A., Immel S., Lichtenthaler F.W., Hall B.G.,
RA   Pikis A.;
RT   "Metabolism of sucrose and its five linkage-isomeric alpha-D-glucosyl-
RT   D-fructoses by Klebsiella pneumoniae. Participation and properties of
RT   sucrose-6-phosphate hydrolase and phospho-alpha-glucosidase.";
RL   J. Biol. Chem. 276:37415-37425(2001).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Hydrolyzes a wide variety of 6-phospho-alpha-D-
CC       glucosides including maltose-6'P, isomaltose-6'P, maltitol-6P,
CC       trehalose-6P and the 6'-phosphorylated derivatives of the five
CC       linkage-isomeric alpha-D-glucosyl-D-fructoses: trehalulose-6'P,
CC       turanose-6'P, maltulose-6'P, leucrose-6'P, and palatinose-6'P.
CC       However, sucrose-6P is not a substrate for this enzyme.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Maltose 6'-phosphate + H(2)O = D-glucose 6-
CC       phosphate + D-glucose.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: NAD and a divalent metal ion. Manganese, cobalt and
CC       nickel ions enhance activity whereas magnesium, calcium, and zinc
CC       ions are without effect or inhibitory.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Sucrose isomers metabolism.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By the five linkage-isomeric alpha-D-glucosyl-D-
CC       fructoses, or by maltose or maltitol.
CC   -!- MASS SPECTROMETRY: MW=49254; METHOD=Electrospray; RANGE=1-440;
CC       NOTE=Ref.1.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 4 of glycosyl hydrolases.
