CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Hydrolysis of terminal, non-reducing 1,4-
CC       linked D-glucose residues with release of D-glucose.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: High levels seen in the aleurone and scutellum
CC       after germination, while low levels are found in developing seeds.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Levels increase steadily throughout
CC       imbibition reaching maximum levels at day 7. During germination,
CC       levels increase from day 2, reach maximum levels at day 3 and
CC       decline after day 5.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: BY gibberellin A3 (GA).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 31 of glycosyl hydrolases.
