CC   -!- FUNCTION: Has a role in cell separation where it is required for
CC       the degradation of the cell wall material surrounding the septum
CC       (the septum edging) which must be hydrolyzed before full
CC       separation of the daughter cells can occur. Hydrolyzes 1,3-alpha-
CC       glucan predominantly into pentasaccharides.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Endohydrolysis of 1,3-alpha-D-glucosidic
CC       linkages in isolichenin, pseudonigeran and nigeran.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted. Associates with the cell wall.
CC   -!- PTM: Not-glycosylated.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 71 of glycosyl hydrolases.
