RL   Genes Dev. 16:2497-2508(2002).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Essential for RNA interference (RNAi); double-stranded
CC       RNA induces potent and specific gene silencing. RNAi is mediated
CC       by the RNA-induced silencing complex (RISC), a sequence-specific,
CC       multicomponent nuclease that destroys or silences messenger RNAs
CC       homologous to the silencing trigger.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with Fmr1 to form a ribonucleoprotein (RNP)
CC       complex involved in translation regulation, other components of
CC       the complex are mRpL5, mRpL11, Rm62 and Dcr-1. Interacts with Dcr-
CC       1 to form components of the RISC.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1; Synonyms=C;
