CC   -!- FUNCTION: In higher primates, agouti may affect the quality of
CC       hair pigmentation rather than its pattern of deposition. May act
CC       as a pharmacological antagonist of alpha-melanocyte-stimulating
CC       hormone (alpha-MSH), by altering levels of intracellular cAMP. It
CC       is possible that expression of ASP in particular developmental
CC       compartments might influence human hair or skin pigmentation.
CC       Could well play a role in neuroendocrine aspects of melanocortin
CC       action. May have some functional role in regulating the lipid
CC       metabolism with adipocytes.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in adipose tissue, testis, ovary and
CC       heart and at lower levels in liver, kidney and foreskin.
CC   -!- PTM: Five disulfide bonds are present (Potential).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the agouti family.
