CC   -!- FUNCTION: Causes hair follicle melanocytes to synthesize yellow
CC       pigment (phaeomelanin) instead of black or brown pigment
CC       (eumelanin), and produces hairs with a subapical yellow band on an
CC       otherwise black or brown background when expressed during the mid-
CC       portion of hair growth. It may act as a pharmacological antagonist
CC       of alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (alpha-MSH), by altering
CC       levels of intracellular cAMP. May have an antitrophic action on
CC       migrating melanoblasts.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Epithelial cells of the hair follicles and the
CC       epidermis.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Widely expressed in embryonic and neonatal
CC       skin.
CC   -!- PTM: Five disulfide bonds are present (Potential).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the agouti family.
