CC   -!- FUNCTION: High-affinity uptake of alpha-glucosides such as
CC       maltose, turanose, isomaltose, alpha-methylglucoside, maltotriose,
CC       palatinose, trehalose and melezitose. Acts with the concomitant
CC       transport of protons into the cell (symport system).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By maltose.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the sugar transporter family.
