CC   -!- FUNCTION: Functions in one of three pathways allowing the
CC       biosynthesis of glycine. Precursors for the different pathways
CC       (and enzymes) are glyoxylate (AGX1), serine (SHM1 and SHM2), and
CC       threonine (GLY1).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: L-alanine + glyoxylate = pyruvate + glycine.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Pyridoxal phosphate.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Glycine biosynthesis from glyoxylate.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Present with 339 molecules/cell. Expression levels
CC       higher in stationary phase than in exponential growth phase when
CC       grown in complex medium with glucose.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class-V pyridoxal-phosphate-dependent
CC       aminotransferase family.
