RT   "The ABCs of floral homeotic genes.";
RL   Cell 78:203-209(1994).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable transcription factor involved in the control of
CC       organ identity during the early development of flowers. Is
CC       required for normal development of stamens and carpels in the
CC       wild-type flower. Plays a role in maintaining the determinacy of
CC       the floral meristem. Acts as C class cadastral protein by
CC       repressing the A class floral homeotic genes like APETALA1. Forms
CC       an heterodimer via the K-box domain with either SEPALATTA1/AGL2,
CC       SEPALATTA2/AGL4, SEPALLATA3/AGL9 or AGL6 that could be involved in
CC       genes regulation during floral meristem development.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer, capable of binding to CArG-box sequences.
CC       Forms an heterodimer via the K-box domain with either
CC       SEPALATTA1/AGL2, SEPALATTA2/AGL4, SEPALLATA3/AGL9 or AGL6.
CC       Heterodimerization also seen with some other Agamous-like MADS box
CC       proteins.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Detected early in the floral meristem but
CC       mostly expressed in stamen and carpel primordia.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Negatively regulated by the A class floral homeotic
CC       protein APETALA2 and by others repressors like LEUNIG, SEUSS, SAP
CC       or CURLY LEAF. Positively regulated by both LEAFY and APETALA1.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Mutations in the AG gene result in the replacement
CC       of the six stamens by six petals and of the carpels by a new
CC       mutant flower.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 K-box dimerization domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 MADS-box domain.
CC   -!- CAUTION: Ref.2 sequences differ from that shown due to erroneous
CC       gene model prediction.
