RT   "Comparative studies of the AHP histidine-containing
RT   phosphotransmitters implicated in His-to-Asp phosphorelay in
RT   Arabidopsis thaliana.";
RL   Biosci. Biotechnol. Biochem. 68:462-465(2004).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Functions as two-component phosphorelay mediators
CC       between cytokinin sensor histidine kinases and response regulators
CC       (B-type ARRs). Plays an important role in propagating cytokinin
CC       signal transduction through the multistep His-to-Asp phosphorelay.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with the B-type response regulators ARR1, ARR2
CC       and ARR10.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Strongly expressed in flowers and roots.
CC       Detected also in leaves, siliques and stems.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By salt, cold and drought stress.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: Histidine-containing phosphotransfer domain (HPt) contains
CC       an active histidine that mediates the phosphotransfer.
CC   -!- PTM: The multistep His-to-Asp phosphorelay consists of the
CC       sequential transfer of a phosphate group from the conserved Asp of
CC       the sensor histidine kinase to a His in the HPt domain of the AHP
CC       protein and finally to an Asp in the receiver domain of the
CC       response regulator.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 HPt domain.
