CC   -!- FUNCTION: Ligand-activated transcriptional activator. Binds to the
CC       XRE promoter region of genes it activates. Activates the
CC       expression of multiple phase I and II xenobiotic chemical
CC       metabolizing enzyme genes (such as the CYP1A1 gene). Mediates
CC       biochemical and toxic effects of halogenated aromatic
CC       hydrocarbons. Involved in cell-cycle regulation. Likely to play an
CC       important role in the development and maturation of many tissues.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Efficient DNA binding requires dimerization with another
CC       bHLH protein. In the nucleus, heterodimer of AHR and ARNT.
CC       Interacts with coactivators including SRC-1, RIP140 and ERAP 140,
CC       and with the corepressor SMRT.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: First cytoplasmic, upon binding with ligand
CC       and interaction with a HSP90, it translocates to the nucleus.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in all tissues tested, including
CC       blood, brain, heart, kidney, liver, lung, pancreas and skeletal
CC       muscle.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Induced or repressed by TGF-beta and dioxin in a cell-
CC       type specific fashion. Repressed by cAMP, retinoic acid, and TPA.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 basic helix-loop-helix (bHLH) domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 PAS (PER-ARNT-SIM) dimerization domains.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 PAS-associated C-terminal (PAC) domain.
