CC   -!- FUNCTION: May be important in protein trafficking and/or protein
CC       folding and stablization.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Interacts with NUB1.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear and cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in retina. Specifically
CC       localized to the developing photoreceptor layer and within the
CC       photoreceptors of the adult retina.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in AIPL1 are the cause of Leber congenital
CC       amaurosis type 4 (LCA4) [MIM:204000, 604393]. LCA designates a
CC       clinically and genetically heterogeneous group of childhood
CC       retinal degenerations, generally inherited in an autosomal
CC       recessive manner. Affected infants have little or no retinal
CC       photoreceptor function as tested by electroretinography. LCA
CC       represents the most common genetic cause of congenital visual
CC       impairment in infants and children.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the FKBP-type PPIase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 TPR repeats.
CC   -!- DATABASE: NAME=Mutations of the AIPL1 gene;
CC       NOTE=Retina International's Scientific Newsletter;
CC       WWW="http://www.retina-international.com/sci-news/aipl1mut.htm".
