CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable transcriptional regulator protein that binds to
CC       DNA as dimer and tetramer, but not as a monomer. Binds to G-
CC       doublets in an A/T-rich environment; the preferred motif is a
CC       tandem repeat of ATTGGTTA combined with a TTATTA-box. May be
CC       involved in immune regulation (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimers and homotetramers.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Predominantly nuclear but also cytoplasmic.
CC       Found in nuclear body-like structures and in a filamentous
CC       vimentin-like pattern.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=12;
CC         Comment=Additional isoforms seem to exist;
CC       Name=1a;
CC         IsoId=Q9Z0E3-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=1b;
