CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expression may be restricted to a small number
CC       of scattered cells in most tissues. Highly expressed in a few
CC       cells in the medulla of the thymus. Detected at very low levels in
CC       thymus, lymph node, liver, brain, ovary, lung, testis, kidney,
CC       heart, spleen, bone marrow, skeletal muscle and adrenal gland.
CC       Isoforms 1a to 1d predominate, isoforms 2a to 2d are intermediate
CC       and isoforms 3a to 3d are expressed at extremely low levels.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The L-X-X-L-L repeats may be implicated in binding to
CC       nuclear receptors.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The N-terminal HSR domain is required for localization on
CC       tubular structures (By similarity).
CC   -!- PTM: Phosphorylated.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 HSR domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 PHD-type zinc fingers.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 SAND domain.
