RC   TISSUE=Brain;
RX   MEDLINE=98165844; PubMed=9497389; DOI=10.1074/jbc.273.11.6533;
RA   Dong F., Feldmesser M., Casadevall A., Rubin C.S.;
RT   "Molecular characterization of a cDNA that encodes six isoforms of a
RT   novel murine A kinase anchor protein.";
RL   J. Biol. Chem. 273:6533-6541(1998).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Binds to regulatory subunit (RII) of protein kinase A.
CC       May be involved in establishing polarity in signaling systems or
CC       in integrating PKA-RII isoforms with downstream effectors to
CC       capture, amplify and focus diffuse, trans-cellular signals carried
CC       by cAMP.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Proximal to tubules in nephrons.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;
CC       Name=KL1A;
CC         IsoId=O54931-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC         Note=Isoform KL1B is produced by alternative initiation at
CC         Met-125 of isoform KL1A;
CC       Name=KL2A;
CC         IsoId=O54931-2; Sequence=VSP_004099;
CC         Note=Isoform KL2B is produced by alternative initiation at
CC         Met-125 of isoform KL2A;
CC       Name=KL3A;
CC         IsoId=O54931-3; Sequence=VSP_004097, VSP_004098;
CC         Note=Isoform KL3B is produced by alternative initiation at
CC         Met-125 of isoform KL3A;
CC       Event=Alternative initiation;
CC         Comment=6 isoforms, KL1A (shown here), KL1B, KL2A, KL2B, KL3A
CC         and KL3B, are produced by alternative initiation at Met-1 and
CC         Met-125;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in lung and weakly in thymus
CC       and cerebellum. Little or no expression in liver, heart and
CC       cerebral cortex. All isoforms are expressed in lung, but KL2A and
CC       KL2B isoforms are the principal isoforms in cerebellum.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: RII-alpha binding site, predicted to form an amphipathic
CC       helix, could participate in protein-protein interactions with a
CC       complementary surface on the R-subunit dimer.
