CC   -!- FUNCTION: May anchor the kinase to cytoskeletal and/or organelle-
CC       associated proteins, targeting the signal carried by cAMP to
CC       specific intracellular effectors.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Binds dimer of the RII-beta regulatory subunit of cAMP-
CC       dependent protein kinase.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Associated with particulate fractions.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Predominantly in brain, and to a lesser extent
CC       in adrenal medulla, lung and anterior pituitary.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: The N-terminal region, which is highly basic, is
CC       required for interaction with calmodulin.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: To other AKAP proteins.
