CC   -!- FUNCTION: May assist in the rapid intracellular transport of bile
CC       acids from the sinusoidal to the canalicular pole of the cell.
CC       Have a role in monitoring the intrahepatic bile acid
CC       concentration.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Trans-1,2-dihydrobenzene-1,2-diol + NADP(+) =
CC       catechol + NADPH.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the aldo/keto reductase family.
