CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the reduction of the delta(4) double bond of
CC       bile acid intermediates and steroid hormones carrying the
CC       delta(4)-3-one structure in the A/B cis configuration. Acts
CC       preferentially on bile acid intermediates. Little activity against
CC       steroid hormones.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: A 3-oxo-5-beta-steroid + acceptor = a 3-oxo-
CC       delta(4)-steroid + reduced acceptor.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: 5-beta-cholestan-3-one + NADP(+) = cholest-4-
CC       en-3-one + NADPH.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in AKR1D1 are a cause of neonatal cholestatic
CC       hepatitis [MIM:235555].
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the aldo/keto reductase family.
