CC   -!- FUNCTION: Binds to type I and II regulatory subunits of protein
CC       kinase A and anchors them to the cytoplasmic face of the
CC       mitochondrial outer membrane.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrial outer membrane (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;
CC       Name=1; Synonyms=AKAP149;
CC         IsoId=Q92667-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2; Synonyms=S-AKAP84;
CC         IsoId=Q92667-2; Sequence=VSP_002845, VSP_002846;
CC         Note=May be produced at very low levels due to a premature stop
CC         codon in the mRNA, leading to nonsense-mediated mRNA decay;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: AKAP149 is highly expressed in prostate and
CC       small intestine whereas S-AKAP84 is expressed in kidney, pancreas,
CC       liver, lung and brain. AKAP149 is also expressed in colon
CC       carcinoma.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: RII-alpha binding site, predicted to form an amphipathic
CC       helix, could participate in protein-protein interactions with a
CC       complementary surface on the R-subunit dimer.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 KH domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 Tudor domain.
