CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the NAD-dependent decarboxylation of threo-
CC       isohomocitrate, threo-iso(homo)(2)citrate and threo-
CC       iso(homo)(3)citrate. These three substates are intermediates in
CC       the biosynthesis of alpha-ketosuberate, a precursor to coenzyme B
CC       and biotin in methanoarchaea.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Alpha-ketosuberate biosynthesis; fifth step.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Alpha-ketosuberate biosynthesis; ninth step.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Alpha-ketosuberate biosynthesis; thirteenth (last) step.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Stable at 100 degrees Celsius for 10 min.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the isocitrate and isopropylmalate
CC       dehydrogenases family.
