CC   -!- FUNCTION: Participates in cellular nitrogen metabolism and also in
CC       liver gluconeogenesis starting with precursors transported from
CC       skeletal muscles.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: L-alanine + 2-oxoglutarate = pyruvate + L-
CC       glutamate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Pyridoxal phosphate.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Liver, kidney, heart and skeletal muscles.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By glucocorticoids.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are two isozymes; a cytoplasmic one and a
CC       mitochondrial one.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the class-I pyridoxal-phosphate-dependent
CC       aminotransferase family. Alanine aminotransferase subfamily.
