RT   Sporobolomyces salmonicolor AKU4429.";
RL   J. Mol. Catal., B Enzym. 6:305-313(1999).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the asymmetric reduction of o-substituted
CC       aliphatic and aromatic aldehydes and ketones to an S-enantiomer.
CC       Reduces ethyl 4-chloro-3-oxobutanoate to ethyl (S)-4-chloro-3-
CC       hydroxybutanoate.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An alcohol + NADP(+) = an aldehyde + NADPH.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Inhibited by quercetin and diphenylhydantoin.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimal pH is 5.5 and optimal temperature is 40
CC       degrees Celsius.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the dihydroflavonol-4-reductase family.
