CC   -!- FUNCTION: Probable transporter. Could be involved in the import of
CC       VLCFA-CoA synthetase into the peroxisomal membrane.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Could form an heterodimer with ABCD2/ALDR.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Peroxisomal.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed at low levels with higher
CC       levels in heart, lung, intestine and spleen than in skeletal
CC       muscle, brain, liver and kidney.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Most abundant in embryo. Gradually decreases
CC       during maturation.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By dietary fenofibrate.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ABC transporter family. ALD subfamily.
