CC   -!- PATHWAY: Glycosylation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type II membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum. Its interaction with the substrate UDP-glucose may
CC       occur at the cytoplasmic side of the ER, whereas the steps
CC       utilizing dolichyl beta-D-glucosyl phosphate take place in the
CC       lumen of the ER.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase family 2.
