CC   -!- FUNCTION: Adds the first glucose residue to the lipid-linked
CC       oligosaccharide precursor for N-linked glycosylation. Transfers
CC       glucose from dolichyl phosphate glucose (Dol-P-Glc) onto the
CC       lipid-linked oligosaccharide Man(9)GlcNAc(2)-PP-Dol.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Glycosylation.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Integral membrane protein. Endoplasmic
CC       reticulum (Potential).
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ALG6 are the cause of congenital disorder of
CC       glycosylation type Ic (CDG-Ic) [MIM:603147]; also known as
CC       carbohydrate-deficient glycoprotein syndrome V (CDGS type V or
CC       CDGS V). CDG-Ic is an autosomal recessive disorder biochemically
CC       it is characterized by an accumulation of dolichyl pyrophosphate-
CC       linked Man(9)GlcNAc(2) in the endoplasmic reticulum. Patients have
CC       muscular hypotonia, show a delayed statomotor development and are
CC       mentally retarded.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ALG6/ALG8 glucosyltransferase family.
CC   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
