CC   -!- FUNCTION: The phosphomannomutase activity produces a precursor for
CC       alginate polymerization. The alginate layer causes a mucoid
CC       phenotype and provides a protective barrier against host immune
CC       defenses and antibiotics. Also involved in core-LPS biosynthesis
CC       due to its phosphoglucomutase activity. Essential for biofilm
CC       production (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Alpha-D-mannose 1-phosphate = D-mannose 6-
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate = alpha-D-glucose
CC       6-phosphate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 magnesium per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Alginate biosynthesis; second step.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Lipopolysaccharide biosynthesis.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the phosphohexose mutase family.
