CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the oxidation of guanosine diphospho-D-mannose
CC       (GDP-D-mannose) to GDP-D-mannuronic acid, a precursor for alginate
CC       polymerization. The alginate layer causes a mucoid phenotype and
CC       provides a protective barrier against host immune defenses and
CC       antibiotics.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: GDP-D-mannose + 2 NAD(+) + H(2)O = GDP-D-
CC       mannuronate + 2 NADH.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: The enzyme can be inhibited by GMP, ATP, GDP-D-
CC       glucose and maltose.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: Alginate biosynthesis; fourth step.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer (Potential). According to Ref.6, this enzyme
CC       exists as a homotetramer, but results obtained in Ref.3 and Ref.5
CC       indicate that it is a homohexamer.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the UDP-glucose/GDP-mannose dehydrogenase
CC       family.
CC   -!- DATABASE: NAME=Protein Spotlight; NOTE=Issue 37 of August 2003;
CC       WWW="http://www.expasy.org/spotlight/articles/sptlt037.html".
