OX   NCBI_TaxID=321;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A., SEQUENCE OF 29-38, AND MUTAGENESIS OF HIS-204 AND
RP   TRP-207.
RC   STRAIN=FF5;
RX   MEDLINE=20485586; PubMed=11029455;
RX   DOI=10.1128/JB.182.21.6268-6271.2000;
RA   Preston L.A., Wong T.Y., Bender C.L., Schiller N.L.;
RT   "Characterization of alginate lyase from Pseudomonas syringae pv.
RT   syringae.";
RL   J. Bacteriol. 182:6268-6271(2000).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Depolymerizes alginate by cleaving the beta-1,4
CC       glycosidic bond. Degrades deacetylated polymannuronate alginate
CC       from P.aeruginosa more efficiently than non-deacetylated polyM.
CC       AlgL from P.syringae degrades also its own alginate, which may
CC       indicate a role in cleaving preformed alginate and/or in
CC       determining the length of the alginate polymer.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Eliminative cleavage of polysaccharides
CC       containing beta-D-mannuronate residues to give oligosaccharides
CC       with 4-deoxy-alpha-L-erythro-hex-4-enopyranuronosyl groups at
CC       their ends.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: The monovalent cation sodium enhances activity
CC       but is not absolutely required.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Periplasmic.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimum temperature is 42 degrees Celsius. Optimum
CC       pH is 7.0.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the polysaccharide lyase family 5.
