CC   -!- FUNCTION: The promoter for a critical alginate biosynthetic gene,
CC       algD, encoding GDP-mannose dehydrogenase, is activated only under
CC       conditions reminiscent of the cystic fibrosis lung (i.e., under
CC       high osmolarity), and at least two regulatory genes, algP and
CC       algQ, have been implicated in this activation process.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The C-terminal domain binds to DNA. It is unknown whether
CC       binding is specific or non-specific.
