RL   EMBO J. 7:345-351(1988).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Acid-stable proteinase inhibitor with strong affinities
CC       for trypsin, chymotrypsin, elastase, and cathepsin G. May prevent
CC       elastase-mediated damage to oral and possibly other mucosal
CC       tissues.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Mucous fluids.
CC   -!- DISEASE: The pathologies of several chronic and acute diseases of
CC       the respiratory tract involve an imbalance between the proteases
CC       of cells involved in inflammatary responses and the inhibitors of
CC       these proteases. The inflammation-mediated release of neutrophil
CC       elastase in the lungs of patients whose levels of active alpha-1-
CC       antiprotease are compromised by genetic background, cigarette
CC       smoking, air pollutants, or a combination of all three can result
CC       in severe lung damage and a decreased lifespan. The relatively
CC       small size of this protein, its lack of glycosylation and its
CC       stability make this protein a candidate for use as a therapeutic
CC       agent in diseases mediated by leukocyte elastase-antielastase
CC       imbalances.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 2 WAP-type domains.
