DE   Alliin lyase 2 precursor (EC 4.4.1.4) (Alliinase 2) (Cysteine
DE   sulphoxide lyase 2).
OS   Allium sativum (Garlic).
OC   Eukaryota; Viridiplantae; Streptophyta; Embryophyta; Tracheophyta;
OC   Spermatophyta; Magnoliophyta; Liliopsida; Asparagales; Alliaceae;
OC   Allium.
OX   NCBI_TaxID=4682;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A., PARTIAL SEQUENCE, AND CHARACTERIZATION.
RC   TISSUE=Bulb;
RX   MEDLINE=95070098; PubMed=7979352;
RA   Rabinkov A., Zhu X.Z., Grafi G., Galili G., Mirelman D.;
RT   "Alliin lyase (Alliinase) from garlic (Allium sativum). Biochemical
RT   characterization and cDNA cloning.";
RL   Appl. Biochem. Biotechnol. 48:149-171(1994).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Able to cleave the C-S bond of sulfoxide derivatives of
CC       Cys to produce allicin, thus giving rise to all sulfur compounds
CC       which are responsible for most of the properties of garlic, such
CC       as the specific smell and flavor as well as the health benefits
CC       like blood lipid or blood pressure lowering.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: An S-alkyl-L-cysteine S-oxide = an alkyl
CC       sulfenate + 2 aminocrylate.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Pyridoxal phosphate (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Vacuolar.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: High expression in bulbs, lower expression in
CC       leaves, and no expression in roots.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: The 6 Cys residues of the EGF-like domain are arranged in
CC       a disulfide pattern different from the one found in the canonical
CC       EGFs. The function of this domain is unclear. It may be a binding
CC       site for other proteins or the docking site for a hypothetical
CC       alliinase receptor (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 EGF-like domain.
CC   -!- DATABASE: NAME=Protein Spotlight; NOTE=Issue 39 of September 2003;
CC       WWW="http://www.expasy.org/spotlight/articles/sptlt039.html".
