CC   -!- FUNCTION: May act as a GTPase regulator.
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;
CC       Name=1;
CC         IsoId=Q96Q42-1; Sequence=Displayed;
CC       Name=2;
CC         IsoId=Q96Q42-2; Sequence=VSP_050521, VSP_050522;
CC       Name=3;
CC         IsoId=Q96Q42-3; Sequence=VSP_050523, VSP_050524;
CC         Note=No experimental confirmation available;
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ALS2 are the cause of amyotrophic lateral
CC       sclerosis (ALS) [MIM:205100], a neurodegenerative disorder which
CC       is closely related to but clinically distinct from juvenile
CC       primary lateral sclerosis. It is a progressive paralytic disorder
CC       which results from dysfunction of the motor systems comprising the
CC       upper motor neurons of the motor cortex and lower motor neurons of
CC       the brain stem and spinal cord.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ALS2 are the cause of juvenile primary lateral
CC       sclerosis (JPLS) [MIM:606353], a neurodegenerative disorder which
CC       is closely related to but clinically distinct from amyotrophic
CC       lateral sclerosis. It is a progressive paralytic disorder which
CC       results from dysfunction of the upper motor neurons of the motor
CC       cortex while the lower neurons are unaffected.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in ALS2 are the cause of infantile-onset
CC       ascending spastic paralysis (IAHSP) [MIM:607225] which is
CC       characterized by progressive spasticity and weakness of limbs.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 DBL-homology (DH) domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 8 MORN repeats.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 PH domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 5 RCC1 repeats.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 VPS9 domain.
