RT   "Mutations in mouse Aristaless-like4 cause Strong's luxoid
RT   polydactyly.";
RL   Development 125:2711-2721(1998).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Transcription factor involved in skull and limb
CC       development.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Binds DNA.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Nuclear.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Expressed in osteoblasts. Not expressed in
CC       brain, heart, intestine, kidney, liver, muscle, spleen and testis.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed from E8.25 and confined to
CC       mesenchymal cells throughout the embryo development. Expression is
CC       seen at several sites including craniofacial region, first
CC       branchial arch and anterior aspect of the limb bud.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in Alx4 are the cause of Strong's luxoid (lst)
CC       phenotype. At heterozygosity lst is characterized by preaxial
CC       abnormalities of the hindfeet and, very rarely, of the forefeet.
CC       Homozygotes show preaxial polydactyly of all four limbs,
CC       reductions and duplications of the radius, absence of the tibia,
CC       craniofacial defects, reduction of the pubis, and dorsal alopecia.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the paired homeobox family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 homeobox domain.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 OAR domain.
