CC   -!- FUNCTION: Tooth enamel proteins are produced in ameloblasts and
CC       play a role in biomineralization.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted; extracellular matrix.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: This protein sequence was found in 70 kDa-, 20 kDa-
CC       and 18 kDa-rabbit teeth enamel proteins.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Rabbit teeth, in contrast to other species, do not
CC       contain amelogenins, but amelogenin-like proteins. Enamelins and
CC       amelogenin-like proteins share this tooth enamel protein fragment.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the amelogenin family.
