CC   -!- FUNCTION: Receptor for anti-Muellerian hormone.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: ATP + a protein = ADP + a phosphoprotein.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in AMHR2 are the cause of persistent Muellerian
CC       duct syndrome type II (PMDS-2) [MIM:261550]; a form of male
CC       pseudohermaphroditism characterized by a failure of Muellerian
CC       duct regression in otherwise normal males.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the Ser/Thr protein kinase family. TGFB
CC       receptor subfamily.
