CC   -!- FUNCTION: Catalyzes the hydrolysis of short-chain aliphatic amides
CC       to their corresponding organic acids with release of ammonia.
CC       Efficiently hydrolyzes propionamide, acetamide and acrylamide, but
CC       shows a very weak activity with aromatic and longer chain
CC       aliphatic amides.
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Also exhibits in vitro acyl transferase activity,
CC       transferring the acyl moiety of short-chain amides to
CC       hydroxylamine to form hydroxamates (By similarity).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: A monocarboxylic acid amide + H(2)O = a
CC       monocarboxylate + NH(3).
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimum temperature for activity is 55 degrees
CC       Celsius and optimum pH is 7.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the nitrilase superfamily. Aliphatic
CC       amidase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 CN hydrolase domain.
