CC   -!- FUNCTION: Is an aliphatic amidase with a restricted substrate
CC       specificity, as it only hydrolyzes formamide. Probably involved in
CC       the nitrogen metabolism of H.pylori.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Formamide + H(2)O = formate + NH(3).
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Inhibited by iodoacetate. Appears to be
CC       regulated by the fur protein, but this effect is not mediated at
CC       the transcriptional level.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homotetramer.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Contrary to the other amidase amiE, expression of amiF
CC       is not repressed by iron.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimum temperature for activity is 45 degrees
CC       Celsius and optimum pH is 6.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Asp-168 is probably not involved in the catalytic
CC       mechanism, but is probably involved instead in maintenance of the
CC       structural integrity of the amidase.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Expression of the amiF gene is stimulated in a
CC       mutant deficient in arginase activity, suggesting that production
CC       of this enzyme is regulated to maintain intracellular nitrogen
CC       balance in H.pylori.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the nitrilase superfamily. Aliphatic
CC       amidase family.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 CN hydrolase domain.
