RA   Fangman J., Disteche C.M., Manova K., Lacy E.;
RT   "The amnionless gene, essential for mouse gastrulation, encodes a
RT   visceral endoderm-specific protein with an extracellular cysteine-rich
RT   domain.";
RL   Nat. Genet. 27:412-416(2001).
RN   [2]
RP   SEQUENCE OF 300-323 AND 393-453, AND VARIANT MGA1 ILE-41.
RX   MEDLINE=22497784; PubMed=12590260; DOI=10.1038/ng1098;
RA   Tanner S.M., Aminoff M., Wright F.A., Liyanarachchi S., Kuronen M.,
RA   Saarinen A., Massika O., Mandel H., Broch H., de la Chapelle A.;
RT   "Amnionless, essential for mouse gastrulation, is mutated in recessive
RT   hereditary megaloblastic anemia.";
RL   Nat. Genet. 33:426-429(2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: May modulate a bone morphogenetic protein (BMP)
CC       signaling pathway (By similarity). Necessary for efficient
CC       absorption of vitamin B12.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:
CC       Event=Alternative promoter;
CC         Comment=At least 5 isoforms, 1 (shown here), 2, 3, 4 and 5, are
CC         produced by use of alternative promoters;
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in small intestine, colon and
CC       kidney (long isoforms). Detected at lower levels in testis, thymus
CC       and peripheral blood leukocytes (shorter isoforms).
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in AMN are a cause of recessive hereditary
CC       megaloblastic anemia 1 (MGA1) [MIM:261100]; also referred to as
CC       MGA1 Norwegian type. MGA1 is due to selective malabsorption of
CC       vitamin B12. Defects in vitamin B12 absorption lead to impaired
CC       function of thymidine synthase. As a consequence DNA synthesis is
CC       interrupted. Rapidly dividing cells involved in erythropoiesis are
CC       particularly affected.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: The mutations described in Ref.2 all affect the N-
CC       terminus of the protein; shorter isoforms produced from
CC       alternative transcription start sites might still fulfill a role
CC       in embryogenesis. This might explain the discrepancy with the
CC       embryonic lethality of null mutants in mice.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 VWFC domain.
