RT   domain.";
RL   Nat. Genet. 27:412-416(2001).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: May modulate a bone morphogenetic protein (BMP)
CC       signaling pathway. Necessary for efficient absorption of vitamin
CC       B12 (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type I membrane protein (Potential).
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Detected in primitive endoderm at E4.5, and
CC       on the apical surface of the visceral endoderm from E5.5 to E8.5.
CC   -!- DISEASE: Defects in Amn are a cause of defects in the development
CC       of the middle primitive streak region during gastrulation. Embryos
CC       that survive to E10 have headfolds, a beating heart and abundant
CC       posterior mesoderm. However, they lack the mesoderm that produces
CC       limb buds, dermis, muscle, vertebrae and other organs of the
CC       trunk.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Contains 1 VWFC domain.
