CC   -!- FUNCTION: Involved in regulation of AMP concentrations.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: AMP + H(2)O = adenine + D-ribose 5-phosphate.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Allosterically activated by Mg-ATP, and
CC       inactivated by inorganic phosphate.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By cAMP at limiting phosphate concentrations. Repressed
CC       by phosphate.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: AMP nucleosidase binds AMP at the catalytic site,
CC       Mg-ATP at an allosteric regulatory site, and inorganic phosphate
CC       also at a regulatory site.
