CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: RCH(2)NH(2) + H(2)O + O(2) = RCHO + NH(3) +
CC       H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: 2-phenylethylamine + H(2)O + O(2) =
CC       phenylacetaldehyde + NH(3) + H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 copper ion, 2 calcium ions and 1 topaquinone per
CC       subunit.
CC   -!- PATHWAY: 2-phenylethylamine catabolism; initial steps.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Periplasmic.
CC   -!- PTM: Topaquinone (TPQ) is generated by copper-dependent
CC       autoxidation of a specific tyrosyl residue.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the copper/topaquinone oxidase family.
