DE   M1-family aminopeptidase (EC 3.4.11.-) (Pfa-M1).
OS   Plasmodium falciparum (isolate FcB1 / Columbia).
OC   Eukaryota; Alveolata; Apicomplexa; Haemosporida; Plasmodium.
OX   NCBI_TaxID=186763;
RN   [1]
RP   SEQUENCE FROM N.A., SUBCELLULAR LOCATION, AND DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE.
RX   MEDLINE=99094503; PubMed=9879894; DOI=10.1016/S0166-6851(98)00143-1;
RA   Florent I.C.P., Derhy Z., Allary M., Monsigny M., Mayer R.,
RA   Schrevel J.;
RT   "A Plasmodium falciparum aminopeptidase gene belonging to the M1
RT   family of zinc-metallopeptidases is expressed in erythrocytic
RT   stages.";
RL   Mol. Biochem. Parasitol. 97:149-160(1998).
RN   [2]
RP   REVISIONS TO N-TERMINUS.
RA   Florent I.C.P.;
RL   Submitted (OCT-2002) to the EMBL/GenBank/DDBJ databases.
RN   [3]
RP   FUNCTION, ENZYME REGULATION, AND SUBCELLULAR LOCATION.
RX   MEDLINE=22156229; PubMed=12166515;
RA   Allary M., Schrevel J., Florent I.C.P.;
RT   "Properties, stage-dependent expression and localization of Plasmodium
RT   falciparum M1 family zinc-aminopeptidase.";
RL   Parasitology 125:1-10(2002).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Displays aminopeptidase activity with a broad substrate
CC       specificity. Preferentially hydrolyzes L-Lys-AMC but also shows
CC       strong activity against L-Ala-AMC, L-Arg-AMC and L-Leu-AMC.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Inhibited by 1,10-phenanthroline and bestatin.
CC       Activity is not affected by phosphoramidin, EDTA, PMSF, leupeptin,
CC       iodoacetamide or pepstatin.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Expressed in erythrocytic stages.
CC   -!- PTM: The 120 kDa precursor is cleaved in vitro into 96 kDa and 68
CC       kDa forms.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: Optimum pH is 7.4 with activity detected from pH
CC       5.8 to pH 8.6.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M1.
CC   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
