RA   Milligan S.B., Gasser C.S.;
RT   "Nature and regulation of pistil-expressed genes in tomato.";
RL   Plant Mol. Biol. 28:691-711(1995).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Presumably involved in the processing and regular
CC       turnover of intracellular proteins.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Release of an N-terminal amino acid, Xaa-|-
CC       Xbb-, in which Xaa is preferably Leu, but may be other amino acids
CC       including Pro although not Arg or Lys, and Xbb may be Pro.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Release of a N-terminal proline from a
CC       peptide.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 2 zinc ions per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Chloroplast.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: By wounding.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M17.
