CC   -!- FUNCTION: This vacuolar enzyme catalyzes the removal of amino
CC       acids from the N-terminus of peptides and proteins.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Release of an N-terminal amino acid,
CC       preferably a neutral or hydrophobic one, from a polypeptide.
CC       Aminoacyl-arylamides are poor substrates.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Zinc.
CC   -!- ENZYME REGULATION: Inactivated by metal-chelating agents and
CC       specifically activated by Zn(2+) and Cl(-).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homododecamer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Vacuolar.
CC   -!- PTM: After a zymogenic synthesis this vacuolar peptidase might be
CC       processed by proteinase yscA (PEP4).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M18.
