RP   FUNCTIONAL DOMAINS FOR BCV INFECTION.
RC   TISSUE=Intestine;
RX   MEDLINE=97138381; PubMed=8985407;
RA   Benbacer L., Kut E., Besnardeau L., Laude H., Delmas B.;
RT   "Interspecies aminopeptidase-N chimeras reveal species-specific
RT   receptor recognition by canine coronavirus, feline infectious
RT   peritonitis virus, and transmissible gastroenteritis virus.";
RL   J. Virol. 71:734-737(1997).
RN   [3]
RP   RECONSTRUCTION FROM ESTS, AND CONCEPTUAL TRANSLATION.
RA   Jimenez S., Stutz A.;
RL   Unpublished observations (MAY-2003).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Broad specificity aminopeptidase. Plays a role in the
CC       final digestion of peptides generated from hydrolysis of proteins
CC       by gastric and pancreatic proteases. May be involved in the
CC       metabolism of regulatory peptides of diverse cell types and in the
CC       cleavage of peptides bound to major histocompatibility complex
CC       class II molecules of antigen presenting cells. May have a role in
CC       angiogenesis (By similarity). May serve as a receptor for bovine
CC       coronavirus (BCV) in a species-specific manner.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Release of an N-terminal amino acid, Xaa-|-
CC       Xbb- from a peptide, amide or arylamide. Xaa is preferably Ala,
CC       but may be most amino acids including Pro (slow action). When a
CC       terminal hydrophobic residue is followed by a prolyl residue, the
CC       two may be released as an intact Xaa-Pro dipeptide.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type II membrane protein.
CC   -!- DOMAIN: Amino acids 44-234 are essential to mediate susceptibility
CC       to infection with TGEV (in human/bovine chimeric studies).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M1.
CC   -!- CAUTION: This is a conceptual translation, the N-terminus was
CC       extended using an EST sequence, in analogy to ortholog sequences.
