RT   "A mouse aminopeptidase N is a marker for antigen-presenting cells and
RT   appears to be co-expressed with major histocompatibility complex class
RT   II molecules.";
RL   Eur. J. Immunol. 23:2358-2364(1993).
RN   [4]
RP   ENZYMATIC CLEAVAGE OF ANTIGEN PEPTIDES BOUND TO CLASS II MHC.
RX   MEDLINE=96305201; PubMed=8691132;
RA   Larsen S.L., Pedersen L.O., Buus S., Stryhn A.;
RT   "T cell responses affected by aminopeptidase N (CD13)-mediated
RT   trimming of major histocompatibility complex class II-bound
RT   peptides.";
RL   J. Exp. Med. 184:183-189(1996).
CC   -!- FUNCTION: Broad specificity aminopeptidase. Plays a role in the
CC       final digestion of peptides generated from hydrolysis of proteins
CC       by gastric and pancreatic proteases. May be involved in the
CC       metabolism of regulatory peptides of diverse cell types. May have
CC       a role in angiogenesis (By similarity). Found to cleave antigen
CC       peptides bound to major histocompatibility complex class II
CC       molecules of presenting cells.
CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Release of an N-terminal amino acid, Xaa-|-
CC       Xbb- from a peptide, amide or arylamide. Xaa is preferably Ala,
CC       but may be most amino acids including Pro (slow action). When a
CC       terminal hydrophobic residue is followed by a prolyl residue, the
CC       two may be released as an intact Xaa-Pro dipeptide.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 1 zinc ion per subunit (By similarity).
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Homodimer.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Type II membrane protein.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in intestinal tract and
CC       kidney, present in liver, lymph node, spleen, and brain. Found as
CC       well in monocytes, macrophages, dendritic cells, veiled cells and
CC       B cells but not on T cells and thymocytes.
CC   -!- PTM: Sulfated (By similarity).
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to peptidase family M1.
