CC       glycoprotein 330.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Present on cell surface forming a complex with the alpha-
CC       2-macroglobulin receptor heavy and light chains.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Intracellular and associated with cell
CC       surface receptors. Found in the endoplasmic reticulum.
CC   -!- DISEASE: In complex with the alpha-2-MR or gp330, it may have some
CC       role in the pathogenesis of membrane glomerular nephritis.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the alpha-2-MRAP family.
