CC   -!- FUNCTION: May control the transcriptional activity of c-Myc.
CC       Stimulates the activation of E box-dependent transcription by c-
CC       Myc.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Binds via its C-terminal region to the N-terminal region
CC       of c-Myc. Associates with S-AKAP84.
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasmic. Translocates into the nucleus
CC       in the S phase of the cell cycle upon an increase of c-Myc
CC       expression. Found in the mitochondria when associated with S-
CC       AKAP84.
CC   -!- TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Highly expressed in heart, placenta, pancreas,
CC       skeletal muscle and kidney. Also present at low levels in lung.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the AMY1 family.
