CC   -!- CATALYTIC ACTIVITY: Endohydrolysis of 1,4-alpha-glucosidic
CC       linkages in oligosaccharides and polysaccharides.
CC   -!- COFACTOR: Binds 3 calcium ions per subunit.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: Monomer.
CC   -!- DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE: Production of alpha-amylase is hormonally
CC       regulated. Germinating embryos produce the hormone gibberellic
CC       acid, which within 10 hours stimulates the aleurone cells covering
CC       the endosperm of the seed to produce alpha-amylase. The enzyme
CC       then degrades the starch within the endosperm for use by the
CC       developing plant embryo.
CC   -!- INDUCTION: Type B isozyme mRNA is undetectable in unstimulated
CC       cells and increases a hundred-fold after stimulation with
CC       gibberellic acid.
CC   -!- MISCELLANEOUS: There are at least 4 types of alpha-amylase in
CC       barley.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to family 13 of glycosyl hydrolases.
